    /**
     * Structured rules compiled from AI硬规则索引 (summaries + doc pointers).
     *
     * @return list<array{id: string, summary: string, doc: string}>
     */
    public static function rules(): array
    {
        return [
            [
                'id' => 'route_via_hard_rules_index',
                'summary' => 'Before code changes, route mandatory docs via AI硬规则索引.md; do not invent requirements from generic framework folklore.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'weline_ui_theme_first',
                'summary' => 'All storefront/admin visual UI MUST use first-party Weline Theme (Weline UI 2.0) component classes and theme CSS variable tokens; forbid third-party UI kits, hard-coded visual literals, and naked address/region inputs when <w:theme:address> exists.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/开发/Theme开发总指南.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'theme_base_components_token_only',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for Theme/UI development: basic/foundation components (w-button, w-input, w-select, w-textarea, w-field, w-badge, w-alert, w-text, w-menu, w-dialog, w-toast, w-table, and peers in foundation.css / Weline UI 2.0) MUST consume only semantic theme tokens (--weline-theme-*, --color-*, --backend-color-*, plus spacing/radius/shadow tokens). Forbid inventing private hex/rgb/hsl colors, parallel palettes, or component-local color CSS variables for those basics when building or restyling themes. Brand themes may override palette leaves in colors/_*.css only; they must not restyle basic components with hard-coded colors. Inherit the default semantic matrix from variables/_colors.css + colors/_default.css (frontend also loads _default before brand overlays like _ink). COMPLEMENT (do NOT override): theme_inverse_raised_paper_ink_pin — WO-UI-CONTRAST-INVERSE paper-ink foundation pins on raised panels are architecture mechanism, not “forbidden hardcode”; Tokenization MUST NOT rewrite those pins into inverse-remapped text tokens. COMPLEMENT: theme_referenced_tokens_must_resolve — Token-only forbids component-private colors BUT REQUIRES every consumed var to have theme palette/variable leaves (incl. dark). COMPLEMENT (do NOT misread Token-only as “always default chrome”): theme_semantic_severity_tone_required — severity/result/action UI MUST bind data-tone; omitting tone or painting everything quiet/neutral is FORBIDDEN.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/theme-semantic-color-matrix.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'theme_referenced_tokens_must_resolve',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD (closes the false conflict “cannot customize colors” vs “buttons look unthemed”): Weline UI / foundation / module CSS MAY ONLY consume theme semantic tokens—MUST NOT invent component-private color/weight/border variables or hard-code hex. WHEN a component references tokens (color, font-weight, border-width, radius, space, control-height, status/tone bridges, etc.), those leaves MUST exist and resolve in Theme `variables/_*.css` + `colors/_default.css` (+ `_light`/`_dark` or backend counterparts when mode differs) and Foundation bridges (`--weline-theme-*`). FORBIDDEN dangling shells: `var(--token)` / `data-tone` / attributes present but leaf missing, empty, or dark-mode unresolved so computed color/weight fails. FORBIDDEN “fix” by writing component-local colors instead of supplementing theme global leaves. On 审图 / WB-OP: if button/badge/alert color or thickness/weight tokens do not visually apply—FAIL until Theme leaves are filled (declare work_mode; default_theme vs design_theme), then bake/theme:upgrade as needed. Authority: theme-css-variables-only.md「提取必落盘 / 禁止空壳」+ theme-semantic-color-matrix.md. Dual-write host: `~/.cursor/rules/theme-referenced-tokens-must-resolve.mdc`. Complements theme_base_components_token_only, theme_semantic_severity_tone_required, theme_frontend_must_obey_tokens_and_surface_roles, user_image_attachment_triggers_shentu.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/theme-css-variables-only.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'theme_semantic_severity_tone_required',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD for storefront/admin UI that expresses severity, risk, result, or action rank (delete/destroy, fail/blocked, warn/risk confirm, success/pass, info/hint, primary CTA vs secondary/cancel): Agent MUST bind Weline UI `data-tone` on `w-button` / `w-badge` / `w-alert` / `w-text` (and peers) per theme-semantic-color-matrix.md — danger|warning|success|info|primary|secondary|neutral|quiet as the human-readable severity map. FORBIDDEN: shipping all controls at component default / quiet / neutral / primary when their severity differs; inventing private `#hex`/`rgb()` severity palettes or parallel `--token-color-*` leaves instead of matrix tones. NON-CONTRADICTION: Token-only forbids private component colors; theme_referenced_tokens_must_resolve REQUIRES status/tone palette leaves (incl. dark) so marked `data-tone` actually paints—attribute-only without resolving leaves is FAIL. Quiet/neutral remain correct for chrome-only (cancel, icon-only close, muted helper). Dual-write host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/theme-semantic-severity-tone.mdc` (global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host). Complements theme_base_components_token_only, theme_referenced_tokens_must_resolve, weline_ui_theme_first, theme_frontend_must_obey_tokens_and_surface_roles.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/theme-semantic-color-matrix.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'theme_inverse_raised_paper_ink_pin',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD (WO-UI-CONTRAST-INVERSE / abstract surface mechanism): When a LIGHT raised panel (dropdown, drawer, paper chip, dialog body, address picker, language/scope menu, etc.) nests under dark/inverse chrome (`[data-surface=inverse]` / `.w-surface-inverse`), the Agent MUST locally PIN foundation paper-ink literals on that raised root FIRST (canonical pair `#0f1111` / `#565959`, optionally also muted `#666666`) into `--weline-chrome-body-text*` (or equivalent paper locals), THEN bind `--amz-drawer-text` / `--_paper-text` / `--color-text*` / body-text to those locals. FORBIDDEN: seeding paper ink from tokens that inverse already remapped—especially `--color-text-primary`, `--color-text`, `--color-text-light`, or any chain that resolves to on-dark cream under the inverse ancestor (creates cream-on-cream / white-on-white). FORBIDDEN during Tokenization / “strip hardcoded visuals” / auto-literals sweeps: rewriting those foundation pins into `var(--color-text-primary)` (or siblings) and calling it a Token win. ALSO: widget CSS that out-specifies Theme raised rebind MUST keep the same pin pattern or it erases Theme’s paper recovery. Tokenization still owns ordinary component/spacing colors via theme_base_components_token_only + theme-css-variables-only.md; this rule is the contrast EXCEPTION (same class as `@media` literal breakpoints). Verify with contract asserts + Browser WB-OP contrast. EXAMPLES ONLY (not the rule body): mini-cart drawer, header search chip, checkout delivery-panel, account dropdown. Dual-write host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/theme-inverse-raised-paper-ink.mdc` (global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host). Complements theme_frontend_must_obey_tokens_and_surface_roles.',
