            [
                'id' => 'custom_theme_acceptance_new_local_website',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for custom (design) theme acceptance / demo — especially 网站柜子 new-site themes: validate on a NEW local website that selects the theme; FORBID switching the storefront theme of the default or any existing site for acceptance. RECIPE: `website:domain-pool` → pick a ready local subdomain; `website:create --name=… --pool-id=… --code=… --json` (writes weline_websites_website + weline_websites_website_domain); bind with `WebsiteThemeBindingService::bindThemeForWebsite($websiteId,$code,$themeId,0)` (website-scoped `w_websites_theme_application`, backend 网站信息→店面主题); then `cache:clear --no-warm` (+ `server:reload` when workers keep the old site). Deliver/verify at `https://<pool-subdomain>/~site/<code>/` — a bare project host falls back to the default site by design (ProjectHostSiteMount) — always with w_fpc_pierce + _wb_nc. If an existing site was already switched, restore the exact prior reference (theme_id/theme_version_id/content_revision/version_owner_scope/version_owner_store_mode) via ThemeApplicationInterface::save() CAS; FORBID hand SQL; keep the new website as that theme demo/regression site (removal needs user approval). On conflict with the old habit (switching an existing site is faster), THIS RULE WINS. Complements theme_engineer_for_theme_work, feature_delivery_urls.',
