            [
                'id' => 'theme_mechanism_not_foreign_content',
                'summary' => 'HARD ABSTRACT module boundary: Each feature’s layouts/templates are owned by the owning business module (Customer/Product/Checkout/…—login is only an EXAMPLE, not the rule’s scope). Weline_Theme owns theme MECHANISM only: layout discovery, slot hosts, solidification/injection runtime, Theme-owned chrome/widgets/Tokens, and the ability for app/design themes to inherit/override. FORBID Theme 兜底/代持/空挂 other modules’ feature layouts or main-content templates—including required default_injections that make Theme the sole deliverer of a foreign path page’s main content, and moving foreign forms/flows into Theme trees “for convenience”. Correct: owning module keeps layouts+content; appearance customization uses design inheritance (theme_design_must_inherit_not_mutate_source_widgets); foreign modules may inject into Theme chrome empty slots with owning-module JSON. Complements theme_layout_widget_owner. Authority: Theme开发总指南.md §6.0; theme-mechanism-not-foreign-content.md.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/开发/spec/theme-mechanism-not-foreign-content.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'theme_design_must_inherit_not_mutate_source_widgets',
                'summary' => 'HARD when work_mode=design_theme (or any task whose intent is one design theme skin / brand look under app/design/{Vendor}/{theme}): MUST customize via theme inheritance only—put overrides under that design theme (frontend/widgets|layouts|partials same logical key; brand colors/_*.css + variables/_*.css + independent assets/css/{brand}*.css). FORBID mutating upstream/parent theme sources that all themes inherit: app/code/**/view/theme/** (including Weline_Theme default shells), app/code/**/view/statics/css/widgets/**, app/code/**/view/statics/js/widgets/**, and any other app/code theme contribution used as parent baseline—one source edit bleeds to every theme. Prefer Token/brand CSS overlay; override widget PHTML only when structure must change; keep @widget.source declarations and point brand-only CSS at design-owned files when needed. HARD STOP+ASK: if the required look cannot be achieved via design inheritance alone (missing override hook, default CSS that cannot be overridden without fighting `!important`, missing Token/extension point), STOP and ask the user—treat as a framework/default-theme gap; FORBID silently editing upstream app/code to unblock one design skin. Platform-wide widget bugs/features require explicit user-approved work_mode=default_theme (or owning-module widget engineer) + cross-theme regression note—NOT a silent edit while “fixing hanfu/daocharms”. Complements theme_default_forbids_css_important, theme_design_must_not_override_core_runtime_assets, dual_workflow_work_mode_gate, theme_engineer_for_theme_work, theme_design_multi_path_is_inheritance_normal. Authority: 主题开发.md Mode B cascade/inherit process; theme-inheritance-and-file-conventions.md decision table.',
                'doc' => 'dev/ai-command/ai/主题开发.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'theme_design_multi_path_is_inheritance_normal',
                'summary' => 'HARD ABSTRACT: Under a design theme root app/design/{Vendor}/{theme}/, the same logical asset MAY appear at more than one on-disk path—modern {area}/… authoring, compat theme/{area}/… or view/theme/{area}/…, and theme:upgrade publish dual-write into that design tree’s Weline/Theme/view/theme URL namespace. This is theme inheritance + publish layout, NOT accidental duplicate/drift. FORBID reporting those sibling paths as architecture smell, “multi-copy bug”, or cleanup that deletes one side of a live design theme. Author edits under work_mode=design_theme go to the design theme authoritative area path; republish with theme:upgrade. Distinct from true defects (e.g. theme skin parked under an unrelated app/code module templates/ tree with no theme register). Complements theme_design_must_inherit_not_mutate_source_widgets. Authority: theme-inheritance-and-file-conventions.md; 规则/20 §7.',
