            ],
            [
                'id' => 'plan_review_three_lenses',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD umbrella when reviewing, self-reviewing, critiquing, approving, rejecting, or 汇审 any engineering plan (Plan Mode body, repository-root `dev/session/{slug}.md` plan notes, engineering-team plan_id, Codex/other-authored implementation plans): MUST concurrently apply THREE independent review lenses—each MUST actually invoke its required tools/probes; skipping any lens → FORBID 通过. (1) Engineering-rigor lens = plan_review_requires_code_evidence: read plan body + probe on-disk code (Read/Grep/explore)—落地可行性与正确性；禁止空想或凭印象下判. (2) Architecture lens = scheme_requires_architecture_review: verify mechanism + owning_module + not_to_do≥1; classify architecture-grade vs patch-grade—禁止补丁级/热修捷径方案过审. (3) Impact-surface lens = plan_review_requires_impact_surface: HARD Cognition ATTEMPT FIRST (`cognition_search`/`cognition_get_entries` when available) then cascade Weline MCP → host-native to determine IOC/blast radius + smells—FORBID skip-to-Grep while claiming impact reviewed. User-facing review MUST present evidence per lens (工程化发现 / 架构清单 / Cognition证据或cognition_unavailable+爆炸半径与隐患) before 是否通过 LAST (user_facing_verdict_last). Complements and binds the three child rules + plan_complete_self_review_then_implement; does NOT replace any child rule body. EXEMPT pure chat / concept Q&A / verbal direction without a review verdict. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/plan-review-three-lenses.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'plan_review_requires_code_evidence',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD when reviewing, critiquing, approving, rejecting, or 汇审 any engineering plan (Plan Mode body, repository-root `dev/session/{slug}.md` plan notes, engineering-team plan_id, Codex/other-authored implementation plans)—engineering-rigor lens under plan_review_three_lenses: (1) READ the plan body (背景/方案/细节—paths, symbols, steps, acceptance)—FORBID judging from title/summary/chat impression alone; (2) PROBE current on-disk code with host Read/Grep/explore for every named file/symbol/extension-point/data-flow—FORBID memory, stale sessions, or “应该如此” speculation (空想); (3) user-facing review MUST present evidence first (plan clause ↔ probed path/symbol/behavior, gaps, risks); insufficient probe → only 「未探测，暂不结论」—FORBID pretending the review is complete; (4) 是否通过 MUST be LAST: write 通过 / 不通过 / 有条件通过 (plus short conditions) ONLY at the end of the review reply—FORBID opening or mid-reply pass/fail before evidence; (5) FORBID unprobed phrases like 「一般会…」「框架通常…」「应该已经有…」 as verdict basis—disk reality wins and mismatches MUST be named. Complements plan_review_three_lenses, plan_review_requires_impact_surface, scheme_requires_architecture_review, plan_content_focus_only, host_plan_mode_for_planning, task_plan_compliance_review, pm_plan_lifecycle, user_facing_verdict_last; EXEMPT pure chat / concept Q&A / user asks for verbal direction without a review verdict. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/plan-review-requires-code-probe.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'plan_review_requires_impact_surface',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD when reviewing, self-reviewing, critiquing, approving, rejecting, or 汇审 any engineering plan (Plan Mode body, repository-root `dev/session/{slug}.md` plan notes, engineering-team plan_id, Codex/other-authored implementation plans)—impact-surface lens under plan_review_three_lenses; in addition to plan_review_requires_code_evidence: (1) DETERMINE the plan’s IOC / impact blast radius (affected modules/paths/symbols/contracts/tests) and architecture smells/risks (architecture-grade vs patch-grade)—what the plan touches and where it may break; (2) HARD Cognition ATTEMPT FIRST: when Cognition MCP tools are available in the session, MUST actually invoke `cognition_search` and/or `cognition_get_entries` (scoped to plan-named paths/symbols/modules/R relations) BEFORE any Weline MCP or host-native impact probe—FORBID skipping Cognition and going straight to Read/Grep/explore while claiming impact reviewed; FORBID treating full Whole-Index Overview as mandatory for every review; only after a real Cognition call returns empty/unusable OR Cognition is unavailable (MUST write `cognition_unavailable:<reason>`) may fall back to Weline MCP (`search_project_knowledge` / `resolve_task_context` / `get_indexed_document`), then host-native Read/Grep/explore; (3) user-facing review MUST name tier(s) used (cognition|mcp|native) AND show Cognition evidence (tool+query+key hits/entry ids) or the `cognition_unavailable` reason, then blast radius + smells/risks, before 是否通过; smells are reported for user adjudication—FORBID silently expanding fix scope; (4) when the plan names code or durable-doc touches but ALL three tiers fail to produce usable impact evidence → only 「未探测影响面，暂不结论」—FORBID pass; (5) FORBID skipping the Cognition attempt (when available) yet claiming impact was reviewed; FORBID using Cognition to replace prepare_project/hard_constraints. Complements plan_review_three_lenses, plan_review_requires_code_evidence, scheme_requires_architecture_review, plan_complete_self_review_then_implement, cognition_complements_weline_mcp, requirement_scan_architecture_smell_gate; does NOT replace requirement_cross_layer_impact_gate (plan-authoring impact_surfaces for entity+field asks). EXEMPT pure chat / concept Q&A / verbal direction without a review verdict. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/plan-review-requires-impact-surface.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'scheme_requires_architecture_review',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD for ANY engineering 方案/scheme before treating it as implementable, approving it, or starting Write—architecture lens under plan_review_three_lenses when a formal plan is under review: (1) SCOPE includes Plan Mode body, repository-root `dev/session/{slug}.md` plan notes, engineering-team plan_id, Codex/other-authored plans, AND any verbal/written implementation scheme that would change code or durable docs—INCLUDING when plan_complexity=simple skipped a formal Plan Mode body; (2) Architecture-style review MUST verify architecture_design_structured fields—named mechanism (Event|Query|Hook|Interface|Taglib|Provider contribution|none:reason) + owning_module (Vendor_Module) + not_to_do≥1 + (when multi-requirement) req_map coverage—and classify architecture-grade vs patch-grade; FORBID approving or implementing “quick patch / hotfix shortcut / want-to-write-whatever” schemes that omit these fields or violate architecture_grade_change_only / architecture_first_for_requirements / framework_decoupled_only; (3) When reviewing a formal plan body, apply as the architecture lens of plan_review_three_lenses IN ADDITION TO plan_review_requires_code_evidence + plan_review_requires_impact_surface (self-review via plan_complete_self_review_then_implement MUST include all three lenses); when no formal plan (simple skip), still MUST record a compact architecture_review checklist {mechanism, owning_module, not_to_do≥1, grade=architecture|patch} and a LAST verdict 通过/不通过/有条件通过 BEFORE any Write; (4) Insufficient architecture structure or patch-grade scheme on an engineering ask → 不通过 or 有条件通过 only—FORBID implement until rewritten architecture-grade; (5) 是否通过 LAST (user_facing_verdict_last). Complements plan_review_three_lenses, plan_review_requires_code_evidence, plan_review_requires_impact_surface, plan_complete_self_review_then_implement, architecture_design_structured, architecture_grade_change_only. EXEMPT correctly graded chat/content_ops; user explicitly asks verbal direction without a review verdict. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/scheme-requires-architecture-review.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'user_facing_verdict_last',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD for every user-facing reply that answers a decisive ask (yes/no, 是不是/能不能/好了吗, pass/fail, which option, status, done-or-not, or any request that expects a clear final conclusion): (1) put evidence / process / explanation in the body FIRST; (2) the FINAL answer/verdict/summary MUST be the LAST lines of the reply—form-matched to the ask (是/不是, 能/不能, 通过/不通过, 已完成/未完成, chosen option, etc.); (3) FORBID mid-reply verdict then long explanation that buries the answer and forces the user to scroll up; (4) FORBID opening with the decisive yes/no/pass when a body follows—opening may orient topic briefly but MUST NOT be the only or primary place of the verdict. Specialization: plan_review_requires_code_evidence clause「是否通过 LAST」. EXEMPT pure chat with no decisive ask; mid-task progress lines that are not the final answer (the turn’s closing reply still ends with the verdict). Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/user-facing-verdict-last.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'user_facing_brief_plain_report',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD for ALL user-facing progress/closeout/plan/status reports (简述 synonyms ONLY: 「简述」/「只要简述」/「说简述」/「说人话」—NOT 「减速」, which is a different concept). Chat MUST be clear+short+decidable—(1) FIXED template only: `问题：` (≤2 short sentences) → `改动：`/`已做：` (≤2) → optional one-line `需你确认：` when a user decision is required → `结论：` LAST with decidable words 已完成|未完成|通过|不通过|需你拍板 (complements user_facing_verdict_last); (2) HARD length budget: default closeout ≤5 lines / ≤约180 Chinese chars before optional 待提交 line—self-compress before send; (3) trigger words IMMEDIATELY summarize THIS plan/session in that template; (4) FORBID path/module/rule-id/workflow/tool-ceremony/evidence-table dumps in chat—Agent MUST self-store detailed reports+evidence (Agent Store or `dev/session/`); (5) IMPLICIT: when user wording is fuzzy about report style, Agent MUST professionally fill clarity/brevity/self-store without asking “要简述还是详细”; pending-commit reminder stays ONE short trailing line. HARD PRIORITY vs acceptance: Accept/RealUC/WBOP ≻ Brief length—Brief ONLY formats chat AFTER the acceptance gate; FORBID using the ≤5-line / ≤180-char budget as a reason to skip 真机实测 or UC闭环; when ¬Accept, 结论 MUST be 未完成 (or equivalent)—FORBID 已完成/通过/PASS/可验收 in Brief while acceptance incomplete; optional ONE short fact in 改动 when Pass (e.g. 「真机WB-OP已过」)—evidence tables still self-store via automation_test_report_durable_evidence. Complements requirement_acceptance_always, real_machine_usecases_not_unit_tests, automation_test_report_durable_evidence. EXEMPT pure chat; user explicitly asks 证据/深挖/完整 diff; mid-task one-liners (turn closeout still uses template+verdict last). Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/user-facing-brief-plain-report.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'requirement_fe_be_scope_analysis',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY at requirement-start on every coding/engineering ask BEFORE code edits: analyze whether this ask needs frontend (phtml/CSS/Theme/JS/Browser UI), backend (Service/Model/API/Controller/Provider), both, or neither. Record fe_be_scope as frontend|backend|both|na with ≥1 concrete bullet each for in-scope sides (paths or surfaces). Forbid coding only one side when analysis shows both (e.g. new field without admin/storefront display, or UI-only without persist/API). Feeds impact_surfaces when entity/field signals fire and ui_skill_decision. Complements requirement_implicit_analysis_skill_decision and requirement_cross_layer_impact_gate.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'requirement_acceptance_always',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD: Every coding/engineering requirement MUST be acceptance-verified BEFORE any user-facing completion/progress report that implies the work is done—never “code only”, never report PASS/已完成/已修好/可验收 to the user before tests ran. Forbidden: mid-implementation “改完了/已落地” chat without evidence; unit-only when Web/UI was touched; asking the user to test. Minimum: (1) ≥1 acceptance item with real evidence (unit/contract and/or runtime probe and/or Browser WB-OP); (2) HARD 真机 Web 测试: Any Web/UI/.phtml/CSS/page touch MUST pass local host Browser WB-OP as real-device web test—navigate → tool-mediated browser_click/browser_fill/browser_press_key → browser_take_screenshot + host Read of the screenshot image (vision) for layout/clip/overflow/density fails (WB-VIS; also run acceptance_phase_requires_shentu when visual)—even when Playwright e2e is skipped under simple classification; (3) work_kind=feature that is NOT simple MUST still obey ui_feature_requires_e2e + plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite; (4) work_kind=feature MUST also close every frozen spec UC via requirement_use_case_closed_loop_acceptance (`covers_use_cases` + passed evidence)—generic e2e PASS without UC coverage does NOT satisfy. FORBIDDEN Web PASS substitutes: curl, contract/unit alone, CDP Runtime.evaluate / getBoundingClientRect metrics, DOM text scrape, Network intercept, in-page fetch, or snapshot YAML alone without screenshot Read—evaluate/metrics may assist diagnosis only; a screenshot that was taken but never Read does NOT count. Incomplete acceptance → only 「代码已改，验收未完成」/「代码已改，需求用例闭环验收未完成」/「代码已改，WebUI 验收未完成」—do not frame as done. HARD PRIORITY: Accept ≻ user_facing_brief_plain_report—Brief never waives 真机; closeout with 结论=已完成/通过 REQUIRES Accept; chat evidence stays self-stored (automation_test_report_durable_evidence)—FORBID host mirrors that dump evidence tables into chat by default; one short 「真机已跑」 fact line is enough in Brief when Pass. Complements requirement_use_case_closed_loop_acceptance, real_machine_usecases_not_unit_tests, browser_operator_self_test, acceptance_phase_requires_shentu, agent_self_verify_before_done, forbid_user_manual_test_handoff, user_facing_brief_plain_report. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/acceptance-before-user-report.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/开发标准与验收.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'requirement_use_case_closed_loop_acceptance',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD for EVERY user coding/engineering requirement that changes product behavior (feature, behavioral bugfix, enhancement—user intent: 任何需求都要用例闭环验收；闭环一定是实际真机测试闭环): freeze UC-* first (feature → owning-module `doc/开发/spec/{slug}.md`; behavioral non_feature that cannot skip clarify MUST still persist minimal UC in that path or SESSION with covers_use_cases). All main-success UCs; alternate/exception UCs once written count too. Before claim done / 汇审 / closeout: (1) Plan `acceptance[]` MUST cover each UC via `covers_use_cases` (orphan UC FORBIDDEN). (2) HARD 真机闭环: every counted UC MUST be closed by real host Browser WB-OP and/or formal Playwright e2e on the live local storefront/admin host—operator clicks/flows + visual when UI; FORBIDDEN to mark a UC passed using only unit/CLI/runtime probe/curl/CDP evaluate without a matching 真机 Browser or e2e pathway. Non-simple → prefer `type=e2e` suite pathway; simple + `e2e_skip_rationale`≥24 → `type=browser` WB-OP still required for that UC. unit/curl/runtime may support but MUST NOT alone close a UC. (3) Every counted UC’s covering acceptance(s) MUST be `status=passed` with non-empty 真机 evidence obeying acceptance_real_business_pathway. (4) Incomplete → only 「代码已改，需求用例闭环验收未完成」—never claim done and never hand UC closeout to the user. (5) Pure doc/gate/infra non_feature with clarify_status=skipped + rationale≥24 → N/A; content_ops_skills_skip_mcp exempt. Complements requirement_clarify_use_case_spec, requirement_acceptance_always, real_machine_usecases_not_unit_tests, browser_operator_self_test, plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite, agent_self_verify_before_done, forbid_user_manual_test_handoff.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'real_machine_usecases_not_unit_tests',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD (UT≠交付): Engineering plans and requirement delivery MUST list and EXECUTE real-machine use cases (UC) on the live local host (CLI/DB/disk/Browser WB-OP as the UC requires)—真机 UC is the delivery gate. Contract tests / PHPUnit / static source contracts ONLY lock code correctness and invariants; they MUST NOT substitute requirement UC acceptance or any user-facing 「已完成/PASS/可验收」claim. FORBIDDEN: reporting feature/delivery done after only “N tests passed” / green contracts when the plan named real-machine UCs; FORBIDDEN omitting UC list from engineering plans that change product behavior. Web/UI surfaces still require Browser WB-OP (cache-off, strip automation, screenshot Read). Closeout MUST persist real-run evidence (commands, HTTP/ttfb or shot paths, DB/disk samples) privately under user_facing_brief_plain_report—not unit counts alone; chat stays brief unless user asks 证据. Complements requirement_acceptance_always, requirement_use_case_closed_loop_acceptance, automation_test_report_durable_evidence, plan_content_focus_only. EXAMPLES ONLY (not rule body): dictionary three-area UC-1…UC-5 (collect upgrade / exclusive bags / storefront·admin shell words / no shared downgrade). Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/real-machine-usecases-not-unit-tests.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'requirement_implicit_analysis_skill_decision',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY at requirement-start on every coding/engineering ask BEFORE code edits: (1) Analyze the CURRENT environment for implicit/hidden requirements—existing Taglib/API/Model/Provider tables, ownership boundaries, mapping/config pages already present, data sync/pull needs, overflow/UX debts, coupling risks, and adjacent modules that make the ask incomplete if ignored. Record ≥1 implicit_requirements bullets (use 无/无隐形需求/none only when truly none after analysis). (2) Also run requirement_fe_be_scope_analysis (frontend/backend/both/na). (3) Plan reasonably from that analysis—do not over-build UI for taglib/API wiring; do not skip provider warehouse tables/pull when mapping needs remote warehouses; do not invent parallel controls when Taglib exists. (4) Decide ui_skill_decision=participate|skip FROM the analysis—NOT by blindly forcing prototype+UI on every feature, AND NOT by wrongly skipping when visual work is in scope. participate when layout/interaction/CSS redesign, new visual surface, messy existing page redesign, CSS/主题 intent, humanization/complaint/吐槽 signals, or 审图 is in scope; also force participate when goal/requirements/scope show UI surface signals (see ui_skill_surface_signal_gate). skip only with ui_skill_rationale (≥24 chars) when NO visual signals (e.g. pure Provider/API/Model, replace hand-filled IDs with existing tags, MCP gate-only). When participate: skill_participation MUST include prototype+frontend-design+weline-theme-development and acceptance MUST include type=shentu—prototype and UI MUST actually adjust (not critique-only). Complements requirement_feature_kind_gate, ui_skill_surface_signal_gate, requirement_framework_scrutiny, taglib_before_hand_rolled_controls, shell_provider_business_isomorph.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'requirement_cross_layer_impact_gate',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY engineering gate when goal/requirements show entity+field+change signals (e.g. 给订单增加类型 / add product field): (1) impact_surfaces REQUIRED with subject + layers covering schema_model, service_api, admin_ui, storefront_ui, i18n, tests_e2e (optional event_hook/checkout_flow); each layer status=in_scope|na|out (na/out need note≥8). (2) schema_model must be in_scope; ≥1 of admin_ui|storefront_ui in_scope; service_api/i18n/tests_e2e in_scope or na+note. (3) Reject empty-only implicit_requirements (无/none). (4) Each in_scope layer must be covered by some concrete task. Prefer resolve_task_context.framework_candidates.impact_candidates for paths when MCP is used. Prevents literal single-layer patches. Complements requirement_implicit_analysis_skill_decision and architecture_design_structured. Non-entity asks may omit impact_surfaces.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'ui_skill_surface_signal_gate',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY engineering gate: when goal, requirements, implicit_requirements, scope_paths, user complaints, 审图 context, OR any user image/screenshot attachment classified web_ui|frontend_candidate show visual/UX signals—.phtml/.css paths, view/templates|hooks, theme color/variable CSS, OR keywords/phrases such as 改UI/调样式/页面布局/布局调整/信息架构/审图/线稿/原型调整/CSS/主题/不够人性化/不人性化/被吐槽/难用/太乱/太丑/体验差/humanization—OR simply「有图/附图/粘贴截图」for product UI—REJECT ui_skill_decision=skip and REQUIRE participate with skill_participation including prototype + frontend-design + weline-theme-development plus type=shentu. HARD: 有图（本仓 Web UI）→ 视觉 UI in_scope + 原型必须上场（skills always; complex team also seats 原型+UI+前端+主题开发工程师）. Prototype and frontend-design MUST produce concrete layout/interaction adjustments (not critique-only). Negation phrases like 无布局重设计 do not count as signals and do NOT cancel an attached web_ui image. Pure backend/API/Provider/MCP-gate work without those signals may still skip with rationale. Complements requirement_implicit_analysis_skill_decision, user_image_attachment_triggers_shentu, css_or_theme_requires_ui_prototype_theme_skills.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'feature_add_requires_current_ui_review',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY when a coding/engineering requirement adds or extends a user-visible feature on an existing Web UI surface (admin/CMS/storefront) AND ui_skill_decision=participate (or CSS/layout redesign is in scope): BEFORE inventing layout/placement or writing production CSS/phtml, Agent MUST open/capture the CURRENT live page (Browser cache-off) and run 审图 (dev/ai-command/theme/审图.md) on that current shot—wireframe → prototype placement → frontend-design → theme tokens. If the current UI is already messy/dense/broken hierarchy (乱), redesign that surface as part of the same feature (do not bolt a new widget onto a chaotic page). Complements requirement_implicit_analysis_skill_decision and acceptance_phase_requires_shentu; this rule is the design-time gate on the EXISTING page, not only post-change acceptance. Skip only when ui_skill_decision=skip with rationale that no visual redesign is in scope.',
                'doc' => 'dev/ai-command/theme/审图.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'feature_ui_keep_simple_top_tabs',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for feature Web UI design AND prototype (admin/CMS/storefront): ALL page groupings MUST use TOP-level tabs (Theme/Weline UI `w-tabs` / top tablist)—one primary job per visible pane. Prototype verdict MUST default to top-tab IA, not a single long stacked page. When a page would stack distinct jobs (list + create form + dictionary/settings, progress + config/ops, monitor + edit), SPLIT into top tabs so users switch segments. Content that still needs to appear without owning a tab MUST use click-to-expand cards (`w-disclosure` / equivalent), default collapsed—forbid always-open multi-card walls. Non-compliant dense pages MUST be redesigned to top tabs in the same feature (do not bolt more blocks onto an overloaded page). Prefer top-level tabs over nested dense cards; secondary subtabs only inside the active primary segment. Complements feature_add_requires_current_ui_review, frontend-design/prototype participation, and 审图 density checks.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'acceptance_phase_requires_shentu',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD during verify/acceptance for ANY Web/UI/.phtml/CSS/page change (or ui_skill_decision=participate / visual Browser surface): Agent MUST take at least one acceptance Browser screenshot of the changed surface AFTER interactions, then host-Read that image (vision) and run 审图 (dev/ai-command/theme/审图.md: wireframe → prototype → frontend-design → theme) BEFORE marking visual/WB/shentu acceptance passed. HARD fail-closed on visible clip/overflow/一字竖排/density crush/cut-off labels—MUST fix layout in the same turn, not report PASS. FORBIDDEN: CDP getBoundingClientRect / Runtime.evaluate / snapshot text alone as visual PASS; FORBIDDEN take_screenshot without Read; FORBIDDEN “metrics look fine” while the shot shows crushed UI. Record type=shentu (or WB-VIS evidence naming 审图/线稿/checklist) with the shot path or Read conclusion; weak evidence blocks closeout. When ui_skill_decision=skip AND no visual surface changed, shentu may be na with explicit N/A—still keep unit/probe/browser evidence for wired surfaces. Complements browser_operator_self_test, requirement_acceptance_always, user_image_attachment_triggers_shentu, agent_self_verify_before_done. Host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/acceptance-before-user-report.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'dev/ai-command/theme/审图.md',
