            [
                'id' => 'architecture_first_for_requirements',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for every coding/engineering change: BEFORE code edits, map each understood (and scrutiny-corrected) user requirement to architecture-layer choices in architecture (≥40 chars, all risk levels including trivial) AND architecture_design (architecture_design_structured)—extension mechanism (Event/Query/Hook/Interface/Taglib/none), owning module boundaries, key paths/layers, and what not to invent. Forbid jumping from requirements straight to code patches. Obey requirement_framework_scrutiny, extension_point_before_code, framework_decoupled_only, architecture_grade_change_only.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'architecture_grade_change_only',
                'summary' => 'SERIOUS ERROR / MANDATORY CONTEXT-CARRIED: Every coding/engineering edit MUST be a framework architecture-grade change—not an ad-hoc “write whatever works” patch. BEFORE any Write/StrReplace/ApplyPatch: (1) name mechanism (Event|Query|Hook|Interface|Taglib|Provider contribution|none:reason) + owning_module + not_to_do≥1; (2) put business data/path lists only in the owning module (Provider/contribution/live index/env)—never invent site catalog/SKU/slug matrices inside Framework Runtime/WLS/FPC orchestrators (runtime_orchestrator_no_business_hardcode); (3) FORBID local shortcuts: parallel process caches, hand-rolled Taglib domains, undocumented events, cross-module new Service/Model, paste-fallback arrays “for speed”. Perf/hotfix pressure NEVER waives ownership. CONTEXT CARRY (硬): this rule + hard_constraints MUST stay in the Agent working context via prepare_project.agent_guidance.hard_constraints + MCP mcpInstructions + alwaysApply coldstart; if the turn can no longer see hard_constraints / architecture_grade_change_only (compaction/summary), MUST re-call prepare_project BEFORE further edits—do not code from memory. Complements architecture_first_for_requirements, architecture_design_structured, framework_decoupled_only, runtime_orchestrator_no_business_hardcode. Authoritative: Ai/doc/规则/10 §2 / 规则/30 §6.1; 扩展点选型.md.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/10-工程流程与验收.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'framework_decoupled_only',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY: Every coding/engineering change MUST follow framework information (扩展点选型.md, module doc/, AI硬规则索引, documented Event/Query/Hook/Interface/Taglib) and MUST use a decoupled design. Forbid coupled writes: cross-module new of concrete Service/Model, undocumented event names, hand-rolled controls when Taglib exists, or bypassing published Interface/Query. plan.architecture must state framework basis + decoupling; plan.coupling_findings is required (≥1 entry; use 无/无耦合/none when none). If coupling is discovered during analysis or implementation, record it in coupling_findings and MUST surface a user-facing 「耦合提示」 section in the feature report (never silently ship coupled code).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/扩展点选型.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'runtime_orchestrator_no_business_hardcode',
                'summary' => 'SERIOUS ERROR / MANDATORY: Framework Runtime orchestrators (WlsRuntime, FPC/deferred warmup, Worker READY gates, keep-warm, HotCache bag-prime scheduling, and isomorphic Server/WLS control-plane code) MUST NOT hardcode owning-module business data—catalog/category/product/blog slugs or demo SKUs, merchant-specific storefront paths, locale×path matrices invented as site content, or any other domain entity list that belongs to Product/Theme/Blog/Index/etc. ALLOWED in Runtime: schedule/budget/cap/owner-election, consume FpcWarmupProviderInterface / ViewWarmupContributionProviderInterface / env `wls.worker.fpc_warmup_paths`, and filter by documented route-shape contracts only (e.g. path starts with `/category/`—shape, never `/category/women`). Business path lists MUST be published by the owning module (live nav/tree/index or contribution provider) or explicit env config—never pasted into WlsRuntime as “fallback” arrays. This style (Runtime invents site catalog) is FORBIDDEN even under perf/hot-fix pressure. Complements framework_decoupled_only + architecture/04-performance-budget.md (warmup paths converged away from hardcoded demo catalog). Authoritative: Ai/doc/规则/30-后端与数据.md §6.1; Framework/doc/architecture/04-performance-budget.md.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/30-后端与数据.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'request_context_logic_diagram_must_read_and_sync',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD when the task touches HTTP request context / RequestPipeline / App bootstrap-dispatch / FPC early-hit / storefront Scope freeze / request-period cache bags (R0 RequestContext memo, Process L1, Shared L2, FPC pools) / request-lifecycle events (pre_route_gate, storefront_scope_ready_gate, url_parsed_after, run_before/after, Router before_start/route_*, response_ready, telemetry): (1) BEFORE diagnosing or editing, MUST host-Read the durable trunk diagram `app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/请求上下文逻辑图.md` (classes, params, bags, events → response)—FORBID inventing a parallel chat-only flowchart as authority. (2) WHEN changing stage order, class ownership, bag tiering, early-exit conditions, or listed event names/contracts so the diagram becomes wrong: MUST update that same Markdown (Mermaid + tables) in the SAME change set—FORBID code/doc drift that leaves a stale trunk. (3) Companion memo/Fiber-boundary docs remain valid; they do NOT replace the trunk diagram. Complements architecture_grade_change_only, runtime_orchestrator_no_business_hardcode, docs_reconcile_on_closeout. Authority: 规则/30 §12.1; Framework/doc/3-开发/请求上下文逻辑图.md. Dual-write host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/request-context-logic-diagram.mdc`.',
