            [
                'id' => 'plan_todo_evidence_closeout',
                'summary' => 'Never claim a multi-todo / multi-chapter plan “done/completed” unless EVERY todo/chapter has concrete evidence including its bound pathway e2e PASS (and feature plans also the final e2e-plan-suite). Partial work MUST be reported as “部分完成/代码已改，e2e 未通过” with an explicit unfinished checklist—NEVER as finished and NEVER by asking the user to close remaining test cases. Update module doc/开发日志.md with unfinished items. Marking Cursor todos completed without evidence is forbidden. Complements plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'plan_ledger_progress_and_acceptance',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for every multi-item / multi-chapter engineering plan (计划书): (1) PERSIST the plan as a durable Markdown plan book at dev/session/{slug}.md (FORBID chat-only plans; FORBID module doc/开发/plan.md). It is the live ledger, not a draft: YAML header + task table with plan_id|title|weight|status|progress|acceptance|evidence|accepted_at, status enum pending|in_progress|blocked|awaiting_acceptance|accepted|rework, overall progress = Σ(weight×item_progress)/100, and an explicit unfinished list. (2) ONE ITEM AT A TIME: claim → implement → finish cleanup/dangling references/dead code/unused symbols/config/templates/i18n → run acceptance → write evidence into the plan book → mark accepted + accepted_at → report the plan file path + recomputed overall progress % → only then start the next item. FORBID marking accepted while any cleanup/未完成子项/dangling reference remains; complete cleanup first (no_legacy_code_accumulation_on_change). (3) Every completion/progress report MUST name the plan file path and overall progress percentage; a report without them is not accepted as closeout. (4) Partial work stays in_progress/awaiting_acceptance with an explicit unfinished checklist; never mark accepted or claim done. (5) The plan book is the record of truth; chat summaries are not. Simple single-step tasks may skip the plan book with plan_skipped=simple, but still obey acceptance. Complements plan_todo_evidence_closeout, agent_self_verify_before_done, no_legacy_code_accumulation_on_change, docs_reconcile_on_closeout.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/10-工程流程与验收.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'agent_self_verify_before_done',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY self-verify after implement on every coding/engineering ask (prefer TDD red→green first)—obey requirement_acceptance_always + requirement_use_case_closed_loop_acceptance + acceptance_real_business_pathway: the Agent MUST personally execute verification matching 开发标准验收层级 BEFORE claiming done—(1) pure logic: focused unit/contract tests actually run to PASS; (2) command/API/persist/runtime: real command or API result plus tests; (3) work_kind=feature that is NOT simple: Playwright e2e via `php bin/w e2e:run` MUST PASS for EACH chapter FULL business pathway (not shell/CTA-only smoke) AND finally the plan-level suite (ui_feature_requires_e2e / plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite / acceptance_real_business_pathway)—closeout MUST name durable artifacts (order_uuid/…); (4) ANY page/UI/.phtml/CSS touch needs HARD 真机 Web 测试: host Browser WB-OP with browser_click/fill + snapshot/screenshot Read (unit/curl/Runtime.evaluate alone MUST NOT substitute; obey browser_operator_self_test)—even when e2e is skipped; (5) feature UCs from spec MUST each be covered by passed `covers_use_cases` acceptance. Do not stop after code edits. acceptance status passed|skipped|na REQUIRES non-empty evidence; required e2e/WB only status=passed with strong evidence. If verification incomplete, report only 「代码已改，验收未完成」/「代码已改，e2e 未通过」/「代码已改，真实通路验收未完成」/「代码已改，需求用例闭环验收未完成」—never claim feature done and never hand testing to the user. Complements local_verify_before_change_and_after_deploy (local verify BEFORE the change ships; production re-verification AFTER deploy).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/开发标准与验收.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'no_legacy_code_accumulation_on_change',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for EVERY code / functional-logic change (监工 and Team: alike; business/content operations 内容运营 exempt): a change REPLACES—it MUST NOT stack. (1) SAME CHANGE SET = SAME CLEANUP: when you replace an implementation, old code paths MUST be deleted in the SAME change set, not “left for later” and not kept “just in case”—FORBID leftover dead/unreachable code; superseded branches or feature-flag/if-else double paths (new path added while the old one stays live); deprecated/legacy classes, services, methods, functions, constants, config keys, DI/registry entries; orphaned templates/partials/widget JSON/blocks/hooks/events/routes/SQL migrations or columns no consumer reads; commented-out code blocks; unused imports/use statements, variables, properties, parameters, CSS selectors/tokens, JS module declarations, and i18n entries left behind; duplicate or parallel implementations of the same capability. (2) NO DANGLING REFERENCES: after the cleanup, the removed symbol/file MUST leave zero call sites, registrations, references, or docs claiming it still exists (owner-module docs/i18n/MCP surfaces reconciled in the same change set). (3) CROSS-MODULE: replace/remove the CONTRACT, not just one side—FORBID leaving orphan consumers when the specification changes, and FORBID public interfaces being silently removed without the dependents being migrated (specify the new interface instead). Follow module upgrade gates for schema/route changes. (4) ANY LEGACY PATH THAT MUST STAY: mark it explicitly (docblock @deprecated / #[Deprecated]) with the reason and planned removal, and record it in the closeout unfinished list + module doc/开发日志.md—it MUST NOT silently accumulate. (5) REPORT: the closeout report MUST list what was cleaned up (symbols/files removed) and MUST NOT hide leftovers under an empty “无” unfinished list (aligns plan_todo_evidence_closeout). HARD BOUNDARY vs preserve_dirty_workspace: this rule governs code YOU are replacing—it NEVER authorizes deleting another session’s/user’s uncommitted dirty work, unrelated TODOs/FIXMEs, DB rows, or business data/config to “clean up”, and it never authorizes git checkout/restore/clean/stash. Complements docs_reconcile_on_closeout, plan_todo_evidence_closeout, module_version_bump_gate.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'no_error_masking_or_patch_workaround',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for EVERY code / functional-logic change (监工 and Team: alike; business/content operations 内容运营 exempt): fix the ROOT CAUSE and NEVER conceal an error, NEVER ship a patch on top of a wrong layer. (1) NO NEGATIVE ERROR MASKING—errors MUST surface with the real cause and context (exception chain / log with context / correct HTTP status / UI error state). FORBID empty or silent catch; catch → return null/false/[]/0/default then continue as success; catch → log-only then pretend success; @ suppression, error_reporting(0), hiding display_errors; downgrading an error to warning/notice; rewriting an exception into “no data”; swallowing validation/permission failures; retrying forever so the failure never surfaces; fake data, hidden switches, silent degradation or fallback to a mock to manufacture success; weakening/removing/skipping assertions or tests, editing expectations to match the bug, skip/only/xfail/@ts-ignore/--no-verify/disabling linters or static checks, commenting out validation, deleting failing tests or evidence, or changing only the error text to hide the cause. (2) NO PATCH-STYLE FIX—a fix MUST land on the owning module’s mechanism (Provider / Taglib / Event / Service / Query / config / extension point). FORBID symptom patches: per-site/per-slug/per-id `if` special cases; hard-coded whitelist/blacklist to dodge validation; try/catch wrapped only around the symptom; bypassing Provider/Taglib/Event/Service/Query extension points; editing generated/ or vendor/ artifacts as the fix; duplicating logic instead of fixing the owning mechanism; “temporary” hacks with no owner/expiry/record. (3) SAME CHANGE SET: remove the replaced wrong path and any superseded fallback branch (no_legacy_code_accumulation_on_change); a patch MUST NOT remain “just in case”. (4) HONEST REPORTING: if it still fails or is unverified, report only 「代码已改，验收未完成」/「未修复」 with the real error and blocked reason—FORBID hiding, shrinking, re-labeling or re-stating a failure as done. ALLOWED (not masking): designed degradation that is user-visible, configurable, logged/monitored and documented in not_to_do; validation/permission/idempotent rejections that return explicit error codes; catch that logs and RETHROWS or converts to a user-visible error while preserving the original exception chain; bounded retries with a visible final failure. Complements agent_self_verify_before_done, local_verify_before_change_and_after_deploy, architecture_grade_change_only, no_legacy_code_accumulation_on_change, tester_tests_must_be_real.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/10-工程流程与验收.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'local_verify_before_change_and_after_deploy',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY verification ordering for EVERY code / functional-logic change (applies to 监工 and Team: alike; business/content operations 内容运营 exempt—their own gates apply): (1) LOCAL VERIFY FIRST—before the change may be declared finished, handed over, committed for release, pushed, or deployed, the Agent MUST run the matching LOCAL logic verification on this workspace: real execution of the changed logic (focused unit/contract test to PASS, real command/API/persist result, and WB-OP when a Web/UI surface is touched) with non-empty evidence. FORBID expiring this onto “will verify in production”, onto the user, or onto CI alone; a change is NOT shippable while local verification has not PASSed. (2) PRODUCTION CHANGE ⇒ VERIFY LOCAL, THEN DEPLOY, THEN VERIFY PRODUCTION AGAIN—deploying/releasing to a live site (线上/生产; e.g. SSH weline, aiweline.com, production DB/config, remote publish) is its OWN authorized step that requires: (a) local verification already PASSed this turn with recorded evidence, (b) explicit user authorization for the production operation AND local-first / no-DB-reset / rollback path confirmation (obey runtime_status_query_local_first—FORBID touching production when the user did not say 线上/生产/ssh weline/aiweline.com/预发), and (c) AFTER the release a SECOND verification run AGAINST THE PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT on the same logic pathway (real business-pathway evidence, e.g. durable order_uuid/transaction_no or a real production command result, plus WB-OP on the live host when UI is involved)—deployed ≠ verified. FORBID report shapes: “已上线/已修复” from deploy exit code alone; “本地没问题” substituted for production re-verification; marking the production run as passed/skipped/na without evidence. If the production verification cannot be run, report only 「已上线，线上复验未完成」with the blocked reason—never claim done. Local acceptance workflow itself stays owned by agent_self_verify_before_done / requirement_acceptance_always / acceptance_real_business_pathway / ui_feature_requires_e2e (this rule adds the BEFORE-change gate and the AFTER-deploy production re-verification).',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'browser_operator_self_test',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD 真机 Web 测试 for any Web/UI/.phtml/CSS/page change OR any requirement whose fe_be_scope includes frontend: AI MUST use the host’s real local Browser (WB-OP) on agreed use cases as real-device web test—navigate → tool-mediated browser_click/browser_fill/browser_press_key → browser_take_screenshot of the changed surface → host Read the screenshot image (vision) for layout/clip/overflow/density (WB-VIS) and run acceptance_phase_requires_shentu when visual—covering BOTH (a) visual acceptance AND (b) real operator logic clicks/flows—cache disabled on every open. Playwright e2e (`php bin/w e2e:run`) is ADDITIONAL for non-simple features (ui_feature_requires_e2e); skipping e2e under simple classification does NOT waive WB-OP. FORBIDDEN WB-OP / visual PASS substitutes: unit tests, curl, CDP Runtime.evaluate / getBoundingClientRect metrics alone, DOM text scrape, Network intercept, in-page fetch, snapshot YAML without screenshot Read, or one-off IDE probes as the sole closed-loop evidence (evaluate/metrics may assist diagnosis only). If the host has no interactive Browser or cannot screenshot+Read, report only “代码已改，WebUI 验收未完成”—do not ask the user to test. Obey browser_cache_disabled_on_open, browser_operator_non_preemptive, acceptance_phase_requires_shentu, and requirement_acceptance_always. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/acceptance-before-user-report.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'browser_operator_non_preemptive',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD for host WB-OP and sibling Agent automation (Cursor ide-browser / Simple Browser / Glass / host-equivalent operator browsers, and same-spirit Playwright e2e / other operator surfaces): treat acceptance/automation as a VIRTUAL operator plane that MUST NOT contend with the human for OS/IDE focus, mouse, or keyboard. DEFAULT: run non-preemptively in the BACKGROUND—Cursor omit `position` on `browser_navigate` (background navigation that preserves user focus); FORBIDDEN `position:"active"` / forcing Browser panel or headed Chromium into the foreground while the user works; FORBIDDEN stealing or racing the user’s mouse/keyboard (OS-level input injection, focus-grabbing CDP Input routing into the IDE/desktop, or any operator path that makes the human lose control of pointer/keys). Prefer in-webview / tool-mediated clicks & fills that stay inside the virtual Browser surface. Background ≠ skip: WB-OP remains required (browser_operator_self_test); Playwright stays headless by default (e2e_playwright_headless_default). Exception ONLY when the user explicitly asks to watch / focus the Browser. Complements browser_operator_self_test / browser_cache_disabled_on_open / browser_strip_automation_flags / browser_release_after_delivery / browser_operator_fail_closed_release. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/browser-operator-non-preemptive.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'browser_tab_group_identity',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD when the Agent operates the user\'s external Google Chrome (chrome-devtools or any attached Chrome session—social signup, mailbox, third-party sites): (1) BEFORE navigate/click/fill, open or reuse ONE Chrome tab group whose visible title is the function identity `AI·{功能短名}`—one function, one group, stable so the user and the next turn can find it. (2) Create every page for that function inside that group and operate ONLY those tabs. FORBIDDEN: isolated browser contexts the user cannot see, unlabeled tabs mixed into the user\'s existing strip, or acting on a page you cannot name as a member of the current group. (3) Do not AppleScript-activate Chrome or steal OS focus to build the group; the group must still show on the user\'s tab strip. (4) When that function closes (done, stopped, or abandoned), delete the group and its tabs—closed loop; do not leave it. (5) Cursor built-in Browser WB-OP has no Chrome tab groups: this rule does not apply there (browser_operator_non_preemptive still does). If a tab group cannot be created, STOP—do not pretend an unlabeled tab is the group. Host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/browser-tab-group-identity.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'google_chrome_reuse_before_connect',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD contract when the Agent connects to or operates the user\'s Google Chrome (chrome-devtools, CDP, puppeteer, or any DevTools websocket—social signup, mailbox, GSC, third-party sites): (1) BEFORE any navigate/click/fill/script, Read `~/.cursor/chrome-devtools-grant.json`. (2) If owner_pid is alive AND socket exists, call ONLY the already-attached MCP `user-chrome-devtools`. FORBIDDEN: `puppeteer.connect`, a new websocket to `ws_endpoint` or `127.0.0.1:9222`, another `chrome-devtools-mcp`, `--autoConnect`, or a new `--wsEndpoint`. (3) If the grant is missing or the owner is dead, opening your own socket is STILL FORBIDDEN; call MCP `chrome-devtools` so launcher `chrome-devtools-reuse.mjs` bridges or asks Chrome once. (4) If that MCP fails or `list_pages` is empty, STOP and record a blocker—FORBIDDEN falling back to raw CDP/JS. Each new Chrome debug websocket raises 「要允许远程调试吗」 and Chrome does not remember the choice. (5) Do not dismiss the toolbar control that turns remote debugging off. Cursor built-in Browser WB-OP is outside this contract. Host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/google-chrome-reuse-before-connect.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'ui_feature_requires_e2e',
                'summary' => 'DEFAULT MANDATORY for work_kind=feature: plan MUST include (a) ≥1 chapter pathway acceptance type=e2e per chapter AND (b) plan-level e2e-plan-suite; Agent auto-runs Playwright/`php bin/w e2e:run`; closeout requires ALL e2e status=passed with strong evidence. SIMPLE EXEMPTION: plan_complexity=simple + e2e_skip_rationale≥24 (same criteria as host_plan_mode simple skip) may omit Playwright e2e ONLY IF local Browser WB-OP visual+logic PASS evidence is recorded (requirement_acceptance_always / browser_operator_self_test). curl/CDP/narrative clicks remain e2e_evidence_weak and also WB-weak. NEVER ask the user to test. non_feature (docs/gates/infra with no Web) is exempt from both e2e and WB. Complements plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite, forbid_user_manual_test_handoff, browser_operator_self_test, agent_self_verify_before_done.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for every non-simple engineering feature: (1) EVERY chapter/dev_task hard-binds its own type=e2e that covers that chapter’s FULL functional pathway—Agent writes and auto-runs Playwright before marking the chapter done; (2) AFTER all chapter e2e PASSes, run UNIFIED e2e-plan-suite. Simple features with recorded e2e_skip_rationale obey requirement_acceptance_always via Browser WB-OP instead. Forbid reporting “done” after partial chapters, skipping all verification, or asking humans to manually close test cases. Complements chapter_ut_rt_wb_dl, ui_feature_requires_e2e, plan_todo_evidence_closeout, acceptance_real_business_pathway.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'acceptance_real_business_pathway',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for work_kind=feature (engineering team / 监工 alike): claiming done REQUIRES ≥1 REAL business-pathway acceptance that creates or mutates durable domain evidence—e.g. a real order_uuid / display number, paid/unpaid status flip, persisted row, or equivalent artifact the user can look up—NOT shell-only / CTA-copy / empty-query smoke. FORBIDDEN as sole closeout evidence: (a) opening `/checkout/success?outcome=cancel` without order_uuid and only asserting button text; (b) opening `#orders` and only asserting “no fatal”; (c) template-string UT alone for a payment/order UX feature; (d) e2e that never exercises the frozen main UC steps (submit→cancel/fail→continue-pay→resume, etc.). Shell/smoke specs MAY exist as supplements but MUST NOT replace the real pathway. Closeout report MUST name the concrete artifact ids (order_uuid / transaction_no / …). Incomplete real pathway → only 「代码已改，真实通路验收未完成」—never claim feature done. Complements tester_tests_must_be_real, plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite, agent_self_verify_before_done, requirement_acceptance_always, forbid_user_manual_test_handoff, engineering_team_for_new_requirements.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'tester_tests_must_be_real',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for Team:测试: and any Agent/监工 self-verify: tests MUST be real—do NOT deceive yourself. FORBIDDEN circular pass: invent fake fixtures / hand-crafted JSON / fake Model arrays / stubbed SUT responses, then assert against that invented data (or only against rows you side-inserted bypassing the frozen main UC) and claim PASS. ALLOWED: exercise the real production pathway—formal Playwright runner (`php bin/w e2e:run`), host Browser WB-OP, real register/login (local_dev_test_accounts_self_serve), or fixtures that create durable artifacts THROUGH real services—and assert independently lookup-able evidence (order_uuid / DB / admin UI / display number). Closeout evidence MUST NOT exist only in the test-process memory. Complements acceptance_real_business_pathway, agent_self_verify_before_done, e2e_playwright_formal_runner_only, browser_operator_self_test, browser_strip_automation_flags.',
                'doc' => 'dev/ai-command/ai/工程团队.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'browser_strip_automation_flags',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for Team:测试: / Agent WB-OP and formal Playwright e2e on local/dev acceptance: BEFORE navigating or interacting with any page that may load captcha / reCAPTCHA / human-verification (and preferably on EVERY acceptance Browser open alongside browser_cache_disabled_on_open), STRIP automation-detection flags so the session looks like a real user browser—otherwise cloud captcha will block login/submit and the pathway is not a real test. REQUIRED actions (host-capable subset): (1) clear `navigator.webdriver` via CDP `Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument` / Playwright `context.addInitScript` / equivalent so it is undefined/false BEFORE page scripts run; (2) Playwright formal runner MUST launch Chromium with `--disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled` and MUST NOT keep `--enable-automation` (ignoreDefaultArgs); (3) after open, optionally assert `navigator.webdriver` is falsy before captcha clicks. FORBIDDEN: treating “Human-machine verification failed / reCAPTCHA blocked automation” as an acceptable WB-OP pass or as excuse to skip real login/submit; FORBIDDEN leaving default Playwright/CDP automation markers that trip bot scoring. Scope is this repo’s local/dev acceptance against our own storefront captcha—not a general captcha-bypass exploit guide. Complements tester_tests_must_be_real, browser_operator_self_test, browser_cache_disabled_on_open, local_dev_test_accounts_self_serve, e2e_playwright_formal_runner_only.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'forbid_user_manual_test_handoff',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY: Agent MUST NOT ask the user to test, verify, refresh-and-retry, click through acceptance, OR supply local/dev login credentials for any coding/engineering feature. Forbidden handoff phrases include 请你测试/请刷新后再试/请自行验证/帮我点一下确认/请提供测试账号/请给密码/you can verify/please log in. Local backend defaults to admin/admin; frontend accounts are self-created (local_dev_test_accounts_self_serve). The Agent runs UT/RT, required Playwright e2e when not simple-exempt, AND always required Browser WB-OP for Web touches, closes every frozen spec UC (requirement_use_case_closed_loop_acceptance), records evidence, then delivers. Incomplete acceptance → only report 「代码已改，验收未完成」/「代码已改，e2e 未通过」/「代码已改，需求用例闭环验收未完成」—never claim done and never hand the test-case / UC loop or credential ask to humans. Obeys requirement_acceptance_always + requirement_use_case_closed_loop_acceptance + ui_feature_requires_e2e + plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite + acceptance_real_business_pathway + agent_self_verify_before_done + local_dev_test_accounts_self_serve.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'e2e_playwright_headless_default',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for Agent Playwright e2e (`php bin/w e2e:run` / Playwright): default MUST be headless—no Chromium/UI popup. Prefer bare `e2e:run` (runner defaults headless + PLAYWRIGHT_HEADLESS=1) or explicit `--headless`. Do NOT pass `--headed`/`--ui` unless the user explicitly asks to watch the browser. Complements ui_feature_requires_e2e / agent_self_verify_before_done / forbid_user_manual_test_handoff. Host WB-OP Browser for page acceptance is separate and unaffected.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'e2e_playwright_formal_runner_only',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY: Agent MUST launch Playwright ONLY through the formal runner so browser lifecycle is owned by the runner and cleaned up on exit. Allowed: `php bin/w e2e:run …` (preferred) or `npx playwright test …` with repo `tests/e2e/playwright.config.js` (or module-collected specs under that runner). FORBIDDEN: ad-hoc `node -e` / one-off scripts that call `chromium.launch` / `firefox.launch` / `webkit.launch`, backgrounded fire-and-forget Playwright probes, or leaving `chrome-headless-shell` orphans (audio/CPU leak). Need a new check → add/extend a `.spec.js` under module `Test/e2e` or `test/e2e` and run via the formal runner—do not improvise a disposable browser. Host WB-OP (Cursor ide-browser / Simple Browser) is separate and unaffected. Complements e2e_playwright_headless_default / ui_feature_requires_e2e / browser_release_after_delivery.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'e2e_ai_record_into_module_formal_path',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY when AI authors or records Playwright E2E for regression/acceptance: (1) persist the recorded `.spec.js` under the owning module `test/e2e` or `Test/e2e` with `frontend/` or `backend/` surface dirs—same layout as existing module suites; (2) prefer high-uniqueness selectors (`data-testid` and equivalent stable hooks); weaker CSS/text locators are allowed only when no stable hook exists (expect flakiness); (3) after recording, run ONLY via the formal runner (`php bin/w e2e:run …` or repo `npx playwright test` with `tests/e2e` config)—FORBIDDEN treating ad-hoc `node -e` / `chromium.launch` probes as deliverable E2E. Host WB-OP remains separate for interactive acceptance. Complements e2e_playwright_formal_runner_only / ui_feature_requires_e2e. Example: Checkout continue-pay lands in `Weline_Checkout/test/e2e/frontend/*.spec.js` then `php bin/w e2e:run` that file.',
                'doc' => 'tests/e2e/AI录制与发布门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'full_release_requires_commerce_pathway_e2e',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY before FULL RELEASE / production publish of commerce-affecting stacks (user signals: 全量发布 / core 全量上线 / 购物相关生产同步 / full release): Agent MUST run the frozen shopping pathway suite `php bin/w e2e:run --suite=commerce-release` (manifest `tests/e2e/manifests/commerce-release-gate.v1.json`) to ALL PASS on this machine before claiming shippable. Suite covers curated multi-scope commerce pathways (guest/login cart, checkout, continue-pay, express, HelpPay quick, B2B wholesale scopes, shipping split, payment storefront availability)—NOT every Theme/Admin smoke in the repo. commerce-release uses controllable payment driver (fake_card) for account lifecycle—third-party PayPal wallet hang is NOT a gate PASS condition; true PayPal sandbox is opt-in suite `commerce-paypal-sandbox` (wallet fail-fast ≤45s). Missing required gate credentials MUST FAIL (no skip/fake-green); FORBIDDEN claiming PayPal sandbox verified while only controllable driver passed under the same suite id without declaring it. Incomplete → only report 「发布门禁未过 / commerce-release e2e 未通过」. Complements local_verify_before_change_and_after_deploy / e2e_playwright_formal_runner_only / acceptance_real_business_pathway.',
                'doc' => 'tests/e2e/AI录制与发布门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'automation_test_report_durable_evidence',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY after ANY Agent-run automated acceptance (formal Playwright `e2e:run` / suite, focused PHPUnit that gates a claim, API/CLI pathway probes used as acceptance evidence, WB-OP / cold dig / tpl_perf / runtime pathway probes): Agent MUST collect and PERSIST concrete independently lookup-able evidence DATA from the REAL acceptance run—not only pass/fail counts or “测试完了”. HARD 真机实测数据：when criteria are runtime/perf/Web, MUST capture measured numbers (HTTP status, wall/TTFB/first-render ms, leaf `db_q`/`php_ms`/`include_ms`, request id, screenshot path + Read conclusion). REQUIRED when produced: durable ids such as order_uuid / display order number / transaction_no / payment attempt id / coupon / email / fixture token / entity ids; plus command + exit summary. DEFAULT delivery under user_facing_brief_plain_report: PERSIST privately (Agent Store and/or `dev/session/` evidence notes)—FORBID dumping full evidence tables into user chat unless the user explicitly asks 证据/深挖/完整实测; user chat stays the brief 问题→改法→结论 shape (pass/fail one-liner OK). FORBIDDEN: claiming PASS / “e2e 成功 / 已测过 / 冷测改进” with zero persisted artifacts when the suite exercised cart/checkout/payment/order mutations OR claimed leaf/wall improvements; FORBIDDEN using contract “N passed” alone as storefront cold/leaf PASS. If the run stops before durable rows or cannot obtain measured data, persist that gap explicitly—do NOT imply PASS. Complements user_facing_brief_plain_report / acceptance_real_business_pathway / tester_tests_must_be_real / plan_todo_evidence_closeout / agent_self_verify_before_done / forbid_user_manual_test_handoff / requirement_acceptance_always. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/automation-test-report-evidence.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/10-工程流程与验收.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'browser_cache_disabled_on_open',
                'summary' => 'Every time AI opens or navigates an acceptance Browser for WB-OP/WB-VIS: MUST disable HTTP disk/memory cache BEFORE trusting the page—default browser cache causes FALSE PASS on this-turn CSS/JS/HTML. Cursor: Network.enable → Network.setCacheDisabled({cacheDisabled:true}) → THEN browser_navigate (omit position). HARD FPC pierce: EVERY acceptance navigate URL MUST append install FPC pierce stamp query `w_fpc_pierce=<secret>` via `Weline\\Framework\\Http\\Fpc\\FpcPierceStamp::buildQuerySuffix()` (or read generated/framework/fpc_pierce_secret / env wls.fpc_pierce_secret)—append with `?`/`&` correctly; FORBID stacking a second `?`. Without pierce, public `_wb_nc`/nocache/diag queries MUST NOT storm-MISS or edge-bypass. When this turn changed any static CSS/JS/HTML/theme asset: ALSO append _wb_nc=<unix_ms> (or equivalent cache-bust) on EVERY acceptance navigate AND prove the served asset contains this-turn marker (curl Cache-Control:no-cache / CDP document.scripts fetch cache:no-store / Network response body)—setCacheDisabled alone is NOT enough if a prior cached bundle can still paint. Exception: visitor-path intentional FPC HIT / html-disk probes MAY omit pierce only when explicitly labeled visitor-path. FORBIDDEN: browser_cdp Page.reload / Page.reload({ignoreCache:true}) (reloads ENTIRE Cursor workbench, kills agents). If setCacheDisabled denied: note degrade + pierce+_wb_nc navigate or close+reopen tab—never Page.reload. FORBIDDEN claiming WB-OP PASS after a navigate that skipped cache-disable or pierce (except labeled visitor-path), or after only CDP Runtime.evaluate triggered the UI while operator browser_click was never proven. Clearing whole browser profile cache is NOT required. Never hardcode the pierce secret into rules/docs as a sample value.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'browser_release_after_delivery',
                'summary' => 'After WB-OP (and optional WB-VIS), every user-facing feature/stage report MUST include 「交付地址」, then AI MUST immediately close every acceptance Browser tab/webview opened this turn (Cursor: unlock then browser_tabs close for Glass/Simple Browser/ide-browser; other hosts: quit/close the operator session). Do not leave idle Browser processes. Exception only when the user explicitly asks to keep tabs open. Pure non-UI work that never opened a Browser: N/A.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'browser_operator_fail_closed_release',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY fail-closed Browser lifecycle for host WB-OP (Cursor ide-browser / Simple Browser / Glass and host-equivalent): (1) BEFORE any browser_navigate, curl-probe the literal acceptance URL with hard timeout `curl --max-time 5` (FORBIDDEN 10/15/30s probe budgets) and accept only 200/302/308/401/403—on timeout/DNS/connection failure/malformed Host (token-as-hostname, no resolvable FQDN, missing *.test.weline.com when available) FORBID opening Browser and report only 「代码已改，WebUI 验收未完成」with the probe error. (2) On ANY Browser tool timeout/error/hang/“No browser tab”/stuck lock/spinning navigate: IMMEDIATELY unlock (if locked) then close EVERY acceptance tab opened this turn; optionally run `php bin/w e2e:cleanup-browsers` for automation leftovers; report the blocker—FORBIDDEN waiting indefinitely or leaving lock/tabs while continuing other tools. (3) Navigate retries ≤2 then fail-closed release. (4) FORBIDDEN holding browser_lock across long shell/php/curl work. Complements browser_release_after_delivery (post-delivery close) / browser_operator_self_test / feature_delivery_urls / browser_cache_disabled_on_open—this rule covers MID-RUN hang so the Agent does not freeze the Cursor session.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'cursor_debug_csp_developer_tooling',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for Cursor agent debug ingest (browser fetch to http://127.0.0.1:7277 or http://localhost:7277, including #region agent log): before relying on those debug records, ensure app/etc/env.php sets security.headers.csp_developer_tooling to a CSP fragment that allows connect-src http://127.0.0.1:7277 http://localhost:7277 (example: connect-src http://127.0.0.1:7277 http://localhost:7277). Framework SecurityHeaderPolicyService unions that Env key into response CSP only when DEV or DEBUG and the key is non-empty—never hardcode Cursor localhost into SecurityHeaderDefaults production CSP, never contribute via Extends Security/Csp app defaults, and never expect production (non-DEV and non-DEBUG) responses to include 7277. If CSP console blocks 7277 while debugging, fix the Env key first; do not weaken production CSP baselines.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/安全响应头策略.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'feature_delivery_urls',
                'summary' => 'Every feature completion or stage handoff report MUST end with a 「交付地址」/Delivery URLs section listing every touched frontend/backend page (and API routes when applicable) as probe-verified http(s) Markdown links [label](url). Local default Host MUST be {project_hash}.test.weline.com (example https://p05113ef3.test.weline.com/...). HARD no port: local delivery/report URLs FORBID any `:port` (incl. WLS worker :9555)—managed Nginx serves 80/443; if the portless URL fails the probe, report the blocker instead of adding a port; NEVER use *.weline.test as the primary acceptance Host when *.test.weline.com is available (even if /etc/hosts lists both); NEVER force 127.0.0.1 when *.test.weline.com exists; never omit the section; never host-private pseudo-protocols (e.g. command:simpleBrowser) as the primary link; mark N/A when no UI. HARD FPC pierce: every primary storefront/admin acceptance http(s) URL in 「交付地址」、related_web_urls、planning/session/team reports MUST append install FPC pierce stamp query `w_fpc_pierce=<secret>` via `Weline\\Framework\\Http\\Fpc\\FpcPierceStamp::buildQuerySuffix()` (or read generated/framework/fpc_pierce_secret / env wls.fpc_pierce_secret)—append with `?`/`&` correctly; FORBID stacking a second `?`; FORBID primary delivery links that omit pierce (stale FPC HIT). Exception: visitor-path FPC HIT / html-disk probes MAY omit pierce only when explicitly labeled visitor-path (secondary). HARD RESOLVED-PIERCE: the delivered Markdown links MUST carry the CURRENTLY EFFECTIVE secret as literal characters, not a placeholder such as `<PIERCE>` / `<install_secret>` / `PIERCE`—a placeholder link is a NON-DELIVERED address and clicking it sends a literal token the edge map cannot match (resolves to FPC HIT), i.e. false claim of pierce. Resolve the effective value with FpcPierceStamp::ensureSecret()/readSecret() (env wls.fpc_pierce_secret first, generated/framework/fpc_pierce_secret fallback) and cross-check var/server/nginx/conf/fpc-pierce.map.conf: when those diverge the edge accepts ONLY the map/env value, so a fallback-file secret silently fails while still looking stamped. Prove pierce before delivery: same URL with pierce returns x-wls-fpc-status: MISS (+ cache-control no-store) while without it returns HIT; if both HIT, the stamp is not effective—fix the secret source, do not deliver. Persistent rule text/docs/templates keep the placeholder/method form only (no real secret written into rules, docs, ledgers or git); the transcript-level delivery links carry the resolved value, and the dev-only local stamp is acceptable in delivery since local and production secrets differ. After that section is written, obey browser_release_after_delivery.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/WebUI浏览器验收与交付地址门禁.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'responsive_breakpoints',
                'summary' => 'Web/UI must design tablet≈768 and PC≥1024 (plus 375 when the surface is mobile-relevant) from the start; for visual storefront/admin layouts collect multi-breakpoint evidence when the host can capture screenshots (WB-VIS under module doc/evidence/).',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'image_explicit_width_height_css',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for any storefront/admin/content image work (including <w:file:image>, raw <img>, CMS/Theme file-image nodes): set explicit HTML width+height (or aspect_ratio / layout_width+layout_height that compile to them) for CLS intrinsic ratio, THEN pair with responsive CSS max-width:100%; height:auto (Theme foundation / .w-file-image). Prefer <w:file:image width height|aspect_ratio>; do not ship images without dimensions “because responsive CSS alone is enough”. Cover/object-fit cases may override height in a more specific rule but must still emit width/height for ratio. Aligns with Google CLS guidance.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/FileManager/doc/file-image-cls-尺寸与响应式.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'widget_layout_stability_theme_primitives',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY Theme-level layout stability (CLS): storefront widgets/cards MUST use foundation primitives .w-frame[data-ratio][data-fit], .w-skeleton[data-size=card] for hydrate/lazy shells, and .w-lines[data-lines] for card titles. file:image auto-wraps .w-frame from layout meta (frame=false when caller already frames). Geometry is global via theme-head once per scope×theme×version pack—FORBID per-layout foundation copies, widget-private aspect/pad-lock legislation, or brand hex in foundation. Gate: php bin/w frontend:check-widget-layout-stability; DEV WidgetHtmlHealth missing_layout_frame/skeleton. Complements image_explicit_width_height_css.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/开发/spec/widget-layout-stability.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'media_reference_identity_protocol',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY: Media occupancy identity follows MediaReferenceIdentity.v1. Build ONLY via w_scope(scope?, type, code, other?) (PHP) or window.w_scope (JS)—never hand-paste identity_path or synthesize scope~sku. scope: segments are storage_scope only; sku:/theme:/brand: are identity only. Unbind uses type+scope+code AND. resource.scope on resource_changed is OPTIONAL (auto from request/Ambient; CLI must pass). Swap/clear image = unbind refs only, never delete files; physical delete goes to trash. Common pick: file-manager tag calls w_scope; visual editor sets explicit identity on the tag (instance). Authoritative: FileManager media-reference-identity-protocol.md + skill media-reference-identity.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/FileManager/doc/media-reference-identity-protocol.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'web_images_webp_compressed',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for ALL web-facing raster images — AI/host generation (Cursor GenerateImage, MediaManager AI draw, product/theme/banner/hero/marketing rasters, image-pipeline exports, agent-authored pub/media or design assets) AND ordinary storefront/CMS/blog/theme uploads. Final on-disk format is WebP (.webp, image/webp); prefer output_format=webp and transcode PNG/JPEG returns before delivery (cwebp -q 80 / Pillow / GD imagewebp), updating DB/path refs. Compress to the smallest size that stays visually clear: resize to the real display size (retina ≤2×, never upscale); longest edge ≤1600px content/product, ≤2560px hero/banner; budget ≤200KB content/product, ≤80KB thumb/card, ≤350KB hero, ≤30KB icon/logo; re-inspect after encoding. FORBID uploading camera/generator originals into pub/media or pages — originals are source-only; FORBID large JPG/PNG lasting deliverables. Keep PNG only when (1) user explicitly asks, (2) true alpha required and the consumer cannot take WebP alpha, or (3) favicon/.ico/platform-mandated PNG. Aligns with MediaManager AiDrawService + AiService defaults.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Product/doc/ai/skills/ecommerce-detail-suite/companions/weline-image-pipeline.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'chapter_ut_rt_wb_dl',
                'summary' => 'Multi-chapter delivery (plan_full_pathway_e2e_suite): each chapter is one complete acceptable full-pathway e2e closed loop (Agent auto-runs Playwright for that chapter’s FE/BE logic) and requires UT, RT, WB (WB-OP host Browser operator path + WB-VIS when visual/screenshot-capable), and DL before the next chapter. After all chapters, run the unified plan e2e suite. Mark chapter progress done before opening the next chapter.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_WORKFLOW_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'section_weline_code',
                'summary' => 'Literal <section> and w:slot wrapper="section" require non-empty semantic weline-code; verify with frontend:check-section-code.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/frontend-section-weline-code.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'theme_layout_widget_owner',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY widget placement (REQ-THEME-0036, 2026-09-21/22 user纠偏): (1) SAME module — layouts/partials may <w:widget>/fetch ONLY that module’s own widgets; if already inlined, FORBID also declaring the same module|code in JSON default_injections (layout XOR injection; delete the JSON; mark placement=layout). (2) CROSS module — FORBID layouts/partials from inlining or fetch-calling another module’s widgets; foreign widgets MUST enter ONLY via empty <w:slot> + the owning module’s JSON default_injections (application default injection). Theme layouts/partials may inline <w:widget> only for Weline_Theme-owned widgets. Never both JSON and layout tags for the same widget (double render). HARD presence (required_default_always_present_without_user_deleted): without manual uninstall user_deleted@{versionId}, chosen-path required defaults exist—JSON path bakes into solidified layout templates (slot exists ⇒ bake; missing defaults ⇒ solidification bug; plugin injection ⇒ rebake all themes’ involved layouts). Engineering team: staff 部件开发工程师 (widget_development) for widget/injection waves. Runtime Overlay soft-skips missing/duplicate fills (no storefront 500). Verify: php bin/w frontend:check-theme-layout-widgets (+ frontend:check-required-injection-sibling-fetch when applicable).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/部件开发指南.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'preview_storefront_delivery_parity',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY: Theme editor / theme-preview / visual_editor / preview=1 / editor_mode / workspace-preview MUST execute the SAME business logic and delivery code paths as the live storefront — identical control flow for Hooks, widgets, floats, nested hooks, session-backed context, captcha/quick-add, auto-detect, and other visitor-facing behavior. FORBIDDEN: any preview-only or editor_mode-only early-return, branch, stub, or gate that discards, skips, quiets, or replaces storefront logic/code just because the request is a canvas/iframe (examples FORBIDDEN: CustomerService body-end preview return; Checkout delivery-context skipping quick-add Hook / auto-detect; StoreMusic Hook preview skip). FORBIDDEN: dual implementations where preview uses a stripped path and publish uses the real path. Layout-aware Hook deferral is allowed ONLY when the same yield condition runs on publish AND preview. Pipeline hygiene (skip a throwaway SSR whose HTML cannot keep nested w:slot markers) is OK only if the real fill pass still runs the full storefront logic. Cache bypass and editor diagnostic markers that ADD chrome without removing storefront logic are OK. Missing domain identity (e.g. no PDP product on a layout canvas) may use empty/demo payload WITHOUT skipping the widget/Hook render path itself. Identity authority is separate (see preview-and-runtime-modes.md): visual editor = request params; version live preview = preview-token deserialize; formal storefront = RequestContext/Scope — do not confuse identity sources with delivery parity.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Theme/doc/preview-and-runtime-modes.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'taglib_no_literal_at_static_in_callback',
                'summary' => 'Taglib callback return HTML must not contain literal @static(...); resolve via Template::fetchTagSource / Local::resolveModuleStaticUrl.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Taglib/doc/如何自定义Tag.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'module_i18n_csv_collect',
                'summary' => 'Every module keeps zh_Hans_CN.csv and en_US.csv with aligned source keys; en_US translate column MUST be real English (never empty and never leave Chinese source as the en value); zh_Hans_CN translate column MUST be Simplified Chinese identity (never put English into the zh translate column). After CSV/string changes run php bin/w i18n:collect — claim translation done only after collect + locale spot-check. Ties to active_locale_must_show_target_language: placeholder Chinese in the en_US translate column OR English left in zh_Hans_CN translate column is a hard delivery failure.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/I18n/doc/模块翻译CSV规范.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'frontend_ui_requires_zh_en_csv',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY frontend development convention for ALL 前端/UI/原型/主题开发工程师 seats and Agents: development language defaults to Simplified Chinese. Whenever adding/changing user-visible storefront/admin UI strings: (1) keep Chinese sources in templates/menus/ACL/__()/@lang/<lang>—Chinese-in-source is CORRECT; FORBID English as default source; (2) bilingual display is via module i18n CSV (NOT CSS)—write BOTH i18n/zh_Hans_CN.csv (Chinese identity translate) AND i18n/en_US.csv (real English translate) for every new/changed source in the same turn; FORBID missing CSV rows, English-in-zh column, or Chinese-in-en column; (3) run php bin/w i18n:collect; (4) spot-check the active admin/storefront locale. BEFORE claiming UI done. Engineering team 前端 seat MUST load template_i18n + module_i18n_csv with Theme skills (frontend_development surface). Complements module_i18n_chinese_source_default, module_i18n_csv_collect, backend_admin_ui_requires_frontend_theme_skills.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/I18n/doc/模块翻译CSV规范.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'module_i18n_chinese_source_default',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for ALL modules (admin + storefront) and especially frontend developers: user-visible source phrases MUST be Simplified Chinese by default — templates (<lang>/@lang), PHP __(), menu.xml title, ACL labels, and other i18n sources. Chinese-in-source is CORRECT and expected (this IS the frontend development language). FORBIDDEN: English (or other non-Chinese) as the default source string in templates/menus (that causes zh locale to show English and mixes CSV columns). Bilingual support = Chinese source in code + zh_Hans_CN identity + en_US real English translate column via CSV (see module_i18n_csv_collect / frontend_ui_requires_zh_en_csv)—NOT by rewriting templates to English and NOT via CSS. Display language is separate — when the active/default locale is not Chinese, obey active_locale_must_show_target_language. Proper nouns/tech tokens (ID, HTTP, Cron, SQL) may stay as-is when they are not prose UI copy. When fixing a module that used English sources, convert code sources to Chinese and rewrite CSV keys to Chinese — do not only patch zh CSV with English→Chinese while leaving English in templates.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/I18n/doc/模块翻译CSV规范.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'active_locale_must_show_target_language',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY (rule-level, pairs with module_i18n_chinese_source_default): Source phrases in code/templates remain Simplified Chinese. The rendered UI MUST follow the ACTIVE request locale and/or website DEFAULT language — NOT the source language. If the website default language is en_US (or the visitor is on en_US / any non-Chinese locale), user-visible copy MUST be that locale’s translation (module en_US.csv translate column and/or system dictionary for other locales). FORBIDDEN: leaving Chinese on screen because en_US (or other target locale) still uses Chinese source as the translate placeholder; treating “template is Chinese” as a reason to show Chinese under a non-Chinese locale; rewriting template sources to English to “fix” display. Fix path: keep Chinese sources → write real target-language translations → php bin/w i18n:collect → spot-check the active/default locale page. Applies to storefront and admin whenever locale ≠ zh_Hans_CN.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/I18n/doc/模块翻译CSV规范.md',
