            [
                'id' => 'user_mentions_translation_all_default_website_locales',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY when the user mentions 翻译 / translate / translation as a work request (including a screenshot of leftover source-language chrome): resolve target locales from the DEFAULT website selected languages — WebsiteLanguage::getWebsiteLanguageCodes(Website::ID_DEFAULT) on the LOCAL database (website_id=0; keep zh_Hans_CN+en_US baseline). Translate the asked surface (and any attached untranslated UI copy) into EVERY selected locale with real target-language copy; never leave Chinese source as the translation; never stop at en_US only. OFFICIAL FRAMEWORK MODULES (this monorepo official Vendor under app/code, e.g. Weline_*): git-slim policy — module i18n/ keeps ONLY zh_Hans_CN.csv and en_US.csv; other locales land in the system dictionary (LocaleDictionary / ai:import-csv / AI translate + publishLocale). This is a framework-repo Git policy to avoid bloating the monorepo — NOT a ban on non-framework/third-party modules shipping additional locale CSV files. After zh/en CSV changes run php bin/w i18n:collect. The user may explicitly narrow locales. Do not start Ollama unless the user asked. Query locales locally first (runtime_status_query_local_first).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/I18n/doc/模块翻译CSV规范.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'no_generated_no_routes_xml',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD ABSTRACT: Framework-compiled return-array / template-compile artifacts under `generated/` (routers, hooks, plugins, events, commands, classmap, factories, query_providers, taglibs, widgets, param_schemas, framework/* snapshots, …) and compiled `view/tpl/` MUST NOT be hand-edited by Agent/AI (Write / StrReplace / patch / invent PHP arrays). FORBIDDEN: treating those files as source-of-truth to “fix” by hand. REQUIRED write path ONLY: system upgrade / formal collect·compile commands (examples—not exhaustive: `php bin/w setup:upgrade`, route collect `--route`, event/hook/taglib/widget/command collect, FrameworkCompiler) or Framework Publisher/Writer APIs that persist then `CompiledPhpRegistry::put` — then consumers READ from the process runtime bag, never re-include as a second source of truth. ALSO: never author `routes.xml` (controllers are auto-discovered); end ORM Query chains with `fetch()`/`fetchArray()`. EXEMPT: reading generated files for diagnosis; tests that assert shapes; staging compile trees behind Publisher. Complements CompiledPhpRegistry lifecycle gate. Authority: Framework 开发标准与验收.md; Ai 规则/30.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/开发标准与验收.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'business_forbids_sql_dialect',
                'summary' => 'SERIOUS ERROR / MANDATORY HARD (abstract portable-SQL boundary): Business application code MUST NOT author database-specific SQL dialect. Dialect SQL belongs ONLY in the ORM database bottom layer—`Weline/Framework/Database/Connection/Adapter/**` Connectors (and sibling Adapter Query), plus Framework `Database/Compiler/**` / `Dialect/**` / `Schema/**` compilers that emit portable↔engine SQL. FORBIDDEN in business Service / Model / Repository / QueryProvider / Controller / module Setup Install·Upgrade·Migration / Observer / Plugin (and Framework services that are not the ORM adapter layer): writing or concatenating MySQL/MariaDB/PostgreSQL/SQLite-specific DML/DDL fragments; `match`/`switch`/`if` on driver/type that emits dialect SQL strings; examples of forbidden dialect (not exhaustive)—`ON CONFLICT`, `ON DUPLICATE KEY`, `INSERT IGNORE`, `REPLACE INTO`, `RETURNING` in business SQL, `JSON_EXTRACT` / `->>` / `::jsonb`, `DATE_FORMAT` / `DATE_SUB` / `strftime`, `UNIX_TIMESTAMP` / `FROM_UNIXTIME`, `GROUP_CONCAT`, `IFNULL`/`IF()` as MySQL-only expressions, `FORCE INDEX`/`USE INDEX`, `ENGINE=InnoDB`, `AUTO_INCREMENT`, MySQL backtick quoting as business SQL style, MySQL `LIMIT offset,count`. REQUIRED instead: portable ORM Query API (`where` / `insert` / `update` / Framework upsert·conflict helpers / `fetch`·`fetchArray`), declarative Model schema, and Framework-exposed DialectInterface helpers—never re-implement engine branches in business modules. Gray but not a license for business DML: pure DB-admin introspection tools under dedicated Database/DbManager admin surfaces may need catalog SQL—still FORBIDDEN to copy that pattern into commerce/domain modules. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/business-forbids-sql-dialect.mdc` (see global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/30-后端与数据.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'no_native_js_dialogs',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY for all storefront/admin JS UX: forbid native window.alert / window.confirm / window.prompt (and bare alert/confirm/prompt). Use Theme UI feedback — Weline.UI.toast for notices, Weline.UI.dialog.confirm / Theme.Notice for confirmations. Contract tests SHOULD assert absence of native dialogs on touched templates/scripts. Do not bury this under unrelated generated/routes rules.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/开发标准与验收.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'weline_api_not_raw_fetch',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY: Browser business I/O for first-party admin/storefront MUST use BinQuery as the default and only transport — `Weline.Api.resource|graph|stream → worker/query-bin`. Forbid native fetch/XMLHttpRequest/$.ajax/axios, hand-written /api/framework/query-bin, and business REST URLs. Forbid treating BinQuery as an HTTP-controller fallback (HTTP-first then catch→Api). If Weline.Api is unavailable, degrade locally (empty/offline)—do not invent a second native request channel.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Frontend/doc/Weline.Api使用指南.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'ui_page_controllers_mutations_via_async_binquery',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD for Admin/Frontend feature development (complements weline_api_not_raw_fetch transport + api_rest_in_owning_module Query core): HTTP Controllers MAY only serve UI page requests (render HTML/layout shells for index/edit/view screens). All non-UI operations that create/update/delete or otherwise mutate management data (资料更新) MUST go through async BinQuery — `Weline.Api.resource|graph|stream → worker/query-bin → owning-module QueryProvider` write/read ops. FORBID implementing save/delete/export/bulk-update as Controller post*/get* actions or form posts to Controller endpoints. FORBID the primitive pattern of managing one information domain via multiple Controllers (e.g. separate Index/Edit/Save/Delete Controllers, or a forest of *Controller classes whose job is data I/O). Thin exceptions match api_rest_in_owning_module: multipart/stream, OAuth/token exchange, webhooks, and Framework BinQuery gateway shells. New admin features: page Controllers + QueryProvider ops + async UI calls—not CRUD Controller sprawl. Dual-write host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/ui-page-controllers-mutations-via-async-binquery.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/30-后端与数据.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'admin_manage_ui_requires_humanized_full_ops',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD when building or claiming done on Admin/backend (or first-party manage) UI for a manageable information domain/resource: the delivered manage surface MUST include humanized full lifecycle ops—not a create-only stub. Baseline (unless the domain is truly singleton/immutable or the user explicitly scopes narrower): (1) list with usable find/filter/pagination when multi-row; (2) create; (3) read/view or edit open; (4) update/edit; (5) delete (or domain-safe disable/archive) with confirm; (6) when the list is multi-select capable, batch ops appropriate to the domain (at least batch delete and/or batch status/enable—do not ship checkbox lists with no batch actions). Mutations still obey ui_page_controllers_mutations_via_async_binquery (async BinQuery/QueryProvider)—this rule is about product completeness of the manage UX, not Controller sprawl. FORBID reporting 「已完成」after only add/create (or only list) while edit/delete/batch remain missing for a normal multi-record manage ask. Narrow exceptions: user-stated scope cut; read-only audit/log/dashboard; singleton SystemConfig-style forms (edit-only, batch N/A); immutable append-only ledgers. Complements backend_admin_ui_requires_frontend_theme_skills (chrome) and ui_page_controllers_mutations_via_async_binquery (transport). Dual-write host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/admin-manage-ui-requires-humanized-full-ops.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/30-后端与数据.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'admin_simple_create_edit_via_modal_binquery',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD for Admin/backend (or first-party manage) UI when create/edit is NOT complex (small field set, no multi-step wizard, no large embedded canvases such as heavy address multi-pickers or rich editors that need a dedicated page): open create/edit in a Weline.UI dialog/modal (`data-w-component=dialog` / `Weline.UI.dialog.open`) and submit via async BinQuery (`Weline.Api→query-bin→owning QueryProvider`). FORBID always-expanded inline create/edit forms permanently occupying the list page vertical space. Prefer list + toolbar「新增」/row「编辑」→ modal. Complex exceptions (dedicated edit route or tab OK): multi-step wizards, large address/region canvases, rich text/media composers, or forms the user explicitly scopes as full-page. Complements admin_manage_ui_requires_humanized_full_ops (ops completeness) and ui_page_controllers_mutations_via_async_binquery (transport)—this rule is the default chrome for simple manage CRUD. Dual-write host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/admin-simple-create-edit-via-modal-binquery.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/30-后端与数据.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'no_php_tags_in_comments',
                'summary' => 'Never put <?= or <?php (or short <? open tags) inside comments (//, #, /* */, /** */, HTML <!-- -->). This targets PHP open/close tags in comments only—not ordinary commented-out statements like // $x = 1;. File headers must use literal text/dates (forbid leftover generator templates such as date short-echo in block comments); delete dead template blocks instead of wrapping <?= inside <?php /* ?>...*/.',
                'doc' => self::AUTHORITATIVE_DOC,
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'chinese_comments_friendly_style',
                'summary' => 'New/changed explanatory comments (//, #, /* */, /** */, HTML <!-- -->) and PHPDoc summaries default to Simplified Chinese; keep existing English comments unless the edit rewrites them. Prefer friendly readable code: match surrounding style, clear names, flat control flow, no clever abstraction or industrial boilerplate; add short Chinese comments only where intent is not obvious. Still obey no_php_tags_in_comments.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Framework/doc/3-开发/开发标准与验收.md',
