            [
                'id' => 'content_ops_skills_skip_mcp',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY SKIP-MCP class: content/commerce-ops skills are NOT coding/engineering cold-start. When the user ask is (or clearly routes to) 产品优化/商品优化/详情优化/商详优化/翻译优化/商品翻译/主图优化/规格图优化/修主图/新建文章/写博客/审查文章/文章可行性/精写文章/blog article/规格修复 (or host/repo skills ecommerce-product-optimize, ecommerce-detail-suite, ecommerce-product-image, ecommerce-product-i18n, weline-blog-article), Agent MUST NOT call prepare_project, resolve_skill, get_skill, search_project_knowledge, resolve_task_context, or otherwise load the MCP skill/index package. Authority is host Read of matching `dev/ai-command/**` + `app/code/*/doc/ai/skills/**/SKILL.md` (host Store mirrors are thin pointers only). Do not pull unrelated MCP skills or hard_constraints bodies “just in case”. If the SAME turn also asks framework Theme/PHP architecture coding beyond these scripted content pipelines, only that coding slice requires normal mcp_call_scope prepare_project.',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'preserve_dirty_workspace',
                'summary' => 'CRITICAL / MANDATORY: Preserve every pre-existing tracked, staged, untracked, and ignored dirty change across MCP repair, reload, generation refresh, validation rollback, crash recovery, and ordinary host edits. Host Agent Shell is equally forbidden from git checkout -- path, git restore, git reset, git clean, git stash (or equivalents) to “clean” a workspace, align HEAD, or redo an edit—that wipes local work and is a severe ban. HARD dirty-load: BEFORE any Write/StrReplace/ApplyPatch, host-Read the CURRENT on-disk working-tree file; all edits MUST continue on that live dirty content (already-changed dirty zone). FORBIDDEN: basing patches on HEAD, index, conversation-stale buffers, other-session snapshots, agent-transcript excerpts, or any older baseline and writing them back—that causes cross-session overwrite of each other’s in-progress dirty files. Multi-agent/multi-chat MUST NOT clobber live dirty work with stale versions. Hash drift → fail-closed keep disk; never restore-from-old then overwrite. MCP child processes may only inspect Git; every Git mutation, config/helper injection, pager helper, and force/discard path is forbidden.',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'machine_shared_side_effects_require_workspace_scope',
                'summary' => 'SERIOUS / MANDATORY workspace-scoped machine-shared side effects (multi-repo laptop). Machine-global state includes macOS System/login keychain Local CA trust (`security add-trusted-cert` / delete-certificate) and host MCP bind (`~/.cursor/mcp.json` LEARNING_MCP_BOUND_REPOSITORY, learning-mcp --config path, `cognition --repo`). (1) ALLOW read/write of THIS workspace’s `var/server/_local_ca/**`, `app/etc/ssl/**`, and hosts for THIS workspace’s domains only. (2) Keychain: FORBIDDEN to install/replace a Local CA whose path/fingerprint is NOT this workspace’s `var/server/_local_ca/rootCA.pem`; FORBIDDEN to assume same CN means the same key across sibling repos; FORBIDDEN silent replace when keychain already holds a same-CN different-fingerprint CA—STOP and ask the user which root to keep (replacing breaks sibling HTTPS). WLS runtime MUST NOT `delete-certificate` any same-CN fingerprint except those listed in THIS workspace’s `var/server/_local_ca/retired_sha1_fingerprints.txt` AND proven workspace-issued (this project’s `var/server/_local_ca/local_ca_provenance.json` says `origin=generated` and `shared=false`, plus this project’s DB/leaf records prove it signed our domains)—CAs inherited from the machine-wide `_local_ca` directory, shared with sibling projects, or of unknown/legacy origin MUST be preserved; a retired-list entry ALONE never authorizes deletion. `add-trusted-cert` for THIS repo’s CA requires an EXPLICIT user ask this turn (信任本仓 CA / 修钥匙串 / trust local CA). (3) MCP/Cognition rebind: ensure/prepare may align `~/.cursor/mcp.json` ONLY when the target root equals the CURRENT open workspace root; FORBIDDEN to rebind global Weline/Cognition MCP to a sibling repo while the IDE workspace is another project; cross-repo rebind ONLY when the user explicitly switches project/workspace this turn. (4) Sibling repos MAY run their own servers/domains under their own trees—FORBIDDEN to “fix their HTTPS/MCP” by mutating global state that breaks the current workspace. EXEMPT: pure chat; content_ops_skills_skip_mcp; user explicitly names 修系统 CA / 改绑 MCP 到指定仓 this turn. Complements cognition_complements_weline_mcp (semantic idempotency) and RepositoryScope (server-side bound) but closes the Agent-side hole of rewriting host mcp.json / keychain for the wrong repo.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'concurrent_session_commit_hygiene',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY commit-scope discipline for a shared dirty working tree (multi-agent / multi-chat / MCP refresh share one checkout). (1) Stage ONLY explicit paths you authored this turn (git add -- <path>...); FORBIDDEN git add -A / git add . / git commit -a sweeps. (2) BEFORE commit reconcile the index against your DECLARED change set (git diff --cached --name-only / --stat) and ABORT on any unexpected path. (3) A dirty path that appears mid-task and is NOT in your declared set is another session’s in-flight work: never treat it as your baseline, never edit, stage, commit, or “tidy” it; report path + status instead. (4) Overlapping file: dirty-load the live disk version, then verify per-hunk (git diff -- <file>) that the index holds only your semantics; ambiguous ownership → STOP and ask, never arbitrate for the other session. (5) This rule NEVER authorizes git stash / git checkout -- / git restore <path> / git clean / git reset --hard (see preserve_dirty_workspace); the only allowed un-stage is the index-only git restore --staged <path>. (6) Parallel work MUST prefer isolation — per-session git worktree + own branch; shared-tree concurrent editing is the root cause of cross-session loss. (7) Do not sweep generated artifacts (MCP catalogs, i18n dumps, theme-compiled tpl, var/**) into a commit unless the generating change is yours. (8) Closeout MUST list the paths committed and the foreign dirty paths deliberately left uncommitted. EXCEPTION — user_utterance_commit_ships_dev_and_sites: when the user utterance is the ship command 「提交」 (not negation 别/不要/先别/不用, not merely defining the word), selective staging YIELDS and the agent MUST commit the entire non-ignored working tree in one commit. This exception does NOT authorize stash/checkout/clean/reset, and does NOT apply on any other turn. EXCEPTION — user_utterance_publish_branch_to_sites: 「发布」 (not 「发布主题」) also commits every non-ignored change, split into one commit per function, not one mixed dump.',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'user_utterance_commit_ships_dev_and_sites',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD when the user message uses 「提交」 as the ship command (also 「确认提交」 / 「提交吧」). That utterance IS explicit authorization to commit, push, and update production sites. NOT a trigger: negation or deferral (先别提交 / 不要提交 / 别提交 / 不用提交 / 先不提交 / 不要 commit), discussing or defining the word, or the Agent\'s own 待提交 reminder. Pipeline, in order: (1) Commit ALL non-ignored local working-tree changes in ONE commit (explicit EXCEPTION to concurrent_session_commit_hygiene selective staging and to one-requirement path scope). No empty commit if the tree is clean. Still FORBIDDEN git stash / checkout -- / restore of the worktree / clean / reset --hard; still do not skip hooks; still do not --force. If a path is a credential or secret file, STOP and report that path instead of committing it. (2) Land the commit on branch `dev`: if HEAD is already `dev`, stay; otherwise merge into local `dev` without force and without discarding the other branch. (3) Push `dev` to BOTH remotes this repo declares as Gitee and GitHub (verify `git remote -v`; cabinet convention is `origin` + `github`—do not hardcode URLs or invent a third remote). (4) BEFORE any production SSH write: `php bin/w e2e:run --suite=commerce-release` must be full PASS (full_release_requires_commerce_pathway_e2e); FAIL stops before SSH. (5) Enumerate cabinets under `websites/` by reading `websites/README.md` and each cabinet README this turn. Update ONLY cabinets that declare a production primary SSH host AND an application root. Skip cabinets with no production host. Count a symlink or alias cabinet once. Same host with different application roots are separate updates—do not collapse by IP. Do not hardcode hosts, IPs, roots, or theme names. (6) For each such cabinet, SSH to its primary host, cd its application root, then: `php bin/w maintenance:enable` → `php bin/w core:update -b dev` (literal branch `dev`; FORBID `-b de` or a site name as the branch) → `php bin/w setup:upgrade` (系统更新) → `php bin/w server:reload -r` → `php bin/w maintenance:disable` (disable even if a middle step failed) → `php bin/w theme:update` using the theme name that cabinet binds, or bare `theme:update` when the cabinet says bound-scope update (theme update is a generation switch: build new batch → verify → flip pointer; NEVER run it inside the maintenance window and never open maintenance just for it). Gitignored design themes are NOT uploaded by this step unless the user separately asked to upload theme files. (7) Back up the database only when that cabinet README says this upgrade touches the database; FORBID whole-tree, code, or theme backups the cabinet forbids. (8) Post-check via SSH to 127.0.0.1 with a Host header (production_http_probe_forbids_agent_local_curl)—FORBIDDEN to curl the public FQDN from the agent workstation. (9) Does not waive preserve_dirty_workspace, hook execution, no-force, or UGC/env.php protection. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/user-utterance-commit-ships-dev-and-sites.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'user_utterance_publish_branch_to_sites',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD when the user message uses 「发布」 as its own ship command (also 「确认发布」 / 「发布吧」). NOT a trigger: bare 「发布主题」 / 「发布某主题」 / 「更新主题」 / 「主题更新」 — those ONLY run theme_update_matches_site_cabinet (copy that theme, no core update, no commit, no dual push). Also NOT a trigger: negation (先别发布 / 不要发布 / 别发布 / 不用发布 / 先不发布), discussing or defining the word, or the 「提交」 utterance (that one still makes ONE commit of everything onto branch dev). 「发布」 INCLUDES the theme-publish step. Pipeline, in order: (1) Branch: default is the currently checked-out branch. If the same utterance names a branch, use that branch. FORBID a site name, theme name, or truncated -b de as the branch. (2) Commit ALL non-ignored local changes, split by function (one commit per function; FORBID one mixed dump commit). No empty commit if the tree is clean. Credential/secret files: STOP and report that path, do not commit it. Still FORBIDDEN stash / checkout -- / restore of the worktree / clean / reset --hard; still do not skip hooks; still do not --force. (3) Push that branch to BOTH remotes this repo declares as Gitee and GitHub (verify git remote -v). If the push is rejected, STOP before any production SSH. (4) BEFORE any production SSH write: php bin/w e2e:run --suite=commerce-release must be full PASS; FAIL stops before SSH. (5) Read websites/README.md and each cabinet README / 关系.md this turn. Update ONLY cabinets that declare a production primary SSH host AND an application root. Skip cabinets with no server or an unverified app root. Count a symlink or alias cabinet once. Same host with different application roots are separate updates. Do not hardcode hosts, IPs, roots, or theme names. (6) For each such cabinet, SSH to its primary host, cd its application root, then: maintenance:enable → php bin/w core:update -b <chosen branch> → php bin/w setup:upgrade (系统更新) → server:reload -r → maintenance:disable (disable even if a middle step failed) → theme publish for that cabinet when its 关系.md names a theme (rsync/scp that theme directory with NO --delete, same as 发布主题) → php bin/w theme:update -t <theme> or bound-scope theme:update when the cabinet names no theme (theme update is a generation switch: build new batch → verify → flip pointer; NEVER run it inside the maintenance window). A cabinet with a server but no registered theme still gets core update and system update; do not guess a theme to copy. (7) Back up the database only when that cabinet says this upgrade touches the database. (8) Post-check via SSH to 127.0.0.1 with a Host header. FORBIDDEN to curl the public FQDN from the agent workstation. Does not waive preserve_dirty_workspace, hook execution, no-force, or UGC/env.php protection. Host alwaysApply mirror: ~/.cursor/rules/user-utterance-publish-branch-to-sites.mdc.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'host_editor_rules_mcp_generated_only',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY: Engineering/product rules are owned only by MCP hard-constraints.v1 and authoritative repo docs (Ai/Framework/module doc/). Project-scoped Cursor/Codex/Claude/VS Code host editor rule files (.cursor/rules/*.mdc inside the repo, .cursorrules, CLAUDE.md, .codex/*, .github/copilot-instructions.md, editor-private AGENTS forks, etc.) MUST NOT be hand-authored or directly edited by the Agent as the rule source—switching projects makes those files disappear or diverge. Host editor rule artifacts (including .cursor/rules/weline-mcp-coldstart.mdc and .cursor/hooks.json for learning collection) MUST be generated only by MCP ensure/guidance HostEditorRulesGenerator / HostCursorHooksGenerator; AGENTS.md remains pointer-only for MCP attach. Never treat editor-private rule files as authoritative over prepare_project hard_constraints. EXCEPTION / COMPLEMENT: user-global alwaysApply mirrors under `~/.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (outside the repo) follow global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host—they are NOT a substitute authority, but MUST stay in sync when a global AI rule is added/changed.',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'hc_sl_rule_lifecycle_gate',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD when adding, updating, or deleting MCP hard constraints / HC-SL symbols (HardConstraintsCatalog rules|mcp_operational, HardConstraintsSymbolDsl legend|overrides|formula|gloss, hc-sl.language.v1, or user asks 硬规则入库/新增硬规则/改硬规则/删硬规则/HC-SL/符号规则): (1) BEFORE edits MUST get_skill(hc_sl_rule_lifecycle|weline-hc-sl-rule-lifecycle) and Read `dev/ai-command/ai/HC-SL硬规则生命周期.md` + `app/code/Weline/Ai/Mcp/schemas/hc-sl.language.v1.json` (or HardConstraintsSymbolDsl::languageTable()). (2) ADD: write full summary in Catalog AND formula+gloss_zh (overrides or derive) AND register any NEW atoms in legend() with rule_ids; FORBID summary-only inserts. (3) UPDATE: change summary∧formula∧gloss_zh in the SAME change set; if atoms rename/change meaning, update legend mapping AND every formula/override/mcpInstructions/index/host-mdc reference in the SAME set—FORBID editing prose while leaving stale formulas (脏改). (4) DELETE: remove Catalog entry AND overrides entry AND either delete legend atoms whose rule_ids only pointed at the deleted id OR drop that id from shared atoms’ rule_ids; scrub references; FORBID deleting description/summary while leaving logic symbols or orphan legend rows. (5) After edits MUST run HardConstraintsSymbolDsl::validateCatalogConsistency() (ok) + `php app/code/Weline/Ai/Mcp/tests/hard-constraints-symbol-dsl.php`. Complements global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host (global rules still dual-write host mdc) and prompt_engineer_for_skill_prompt_work (prompt wording ≠ hard-rule lifecycle).',
                'doc' => 'dev/ai-command/ai/HC-SL硬规则生命周期.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY when the user asks to modify 全局规则 / global AI rules / alwaysApply host rules that bind future Agent work across sessions: ALWAYS dual-write BOTH (1) MCP authority—HardConstraintsCatalog rule id + `AI硬规则索引.md` / matching `规则/*.md` / `开发日志.md` (+ contract assertions when required) and (2) Cursor user-global alwaysApply `~/.cursor/rules/{slug}.mdc` (and optional personal Agent Store thin mirror). FORBID MCP-only or host-only one-sided updates. Project `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` remains MCP-generated only (host_editor_rules_mcp_generated_only)—do NOT hand-author project coldstart as a second rule source. Authority order on conflict: prepare_project hard_constraints + repo docs win over `~/.cursor/rules`. Examples already dual-written: `intent_lane_router` ↔ `intent-lane-router.mdc`; `requirement_acceptance_always` ↔ `acceptance-before-user-report.mdc`; `real_machine_usecases_not_unit_tests` ↔ `real-machine-usecases-not-unit-tests.mdc`; `plan_review_three_lenses` ↔ `plan-review-three-lenses.mdc`; `plan_review_requires_code_evidence` ↔ `plan-review-requires-code-probe.mdc`; `plan_review_requires_impact_surface` ↔ `plan-review-requires-impact-surface.mdc`; `scheme_requires_architecture_review` ↔ `scheme-requires-architecture-review.mdc`; `plan_complete_self_review_then_implement` ↔ `plan-complete-self-review-then-implement.mdc`; `plan_implementability_checklist` ↔ `plan-implementability-checklist.mdc`; `requirement_engineering_grade_gate` ↔ `requirement-engineering-grade-gate.mdc`; `requirement_scan_architecture_smell_gate` ↔ `requirement-scan-architecture-smell-gate.mdc`; `learning_rule_extraction_must_be_abstract` ↔ `learning-rule-extraction-abstract.mdc`; `user_facing_verdict_last` ↔ `user-facing-verdict-last.mdc`; `user_facing_brief_plain_report` ↔ `user-facing-brief-plain-report.mdc`; `browser_operator_non_preemptive` ↔ `browser-operator-non-preemptive.mdc`; `theme_inverse_raised_paper_ink_pin` ↔ `theme-inverse-raised-paper-ink.mdc`; `theme_frontend_must_obey_tokens_and_surface_roles` ↔ `theme-frontend-obey-tokens-and-surfaces.mdc`; `theme_semantic_severity_tone_required` ↔ `theme-semantic-severity-tone.mdc`; `theme_design_multi_path_is_inheritance_normal` ↔ `theme-design-multi-path-inheritance-normal.mdc`; `business_forbids_sql_dialect` ↔ `business-forbids-sql-dialect.mdc`; `framework_demos_live_in_weline_demo` ↔ `framework-demos-live-in-weline-demo.mdc`; `production_http_probe_forbids_agent_local_curl` ↔ `production-http-probe-forbids-agent-local-curl.mdc`; `wls_managed_nginx_supports_fpm_origin` ↔ `wls-managed-nginx-supports-fpm-origin.mdc`; `theme_update_matches_site_cabinet` ↔ `theme-update-matches-site-cabinet.mdc`; `plan_ledger_progress_and_acceptance` ↔ `plan-ledger-progress-and-acceptance.mdc`. After dual-write, tell the user a new Agent turn is needed to pick up alwaysApply (FORBID Developer: Reload Window).',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'wls_managed_nginx_supports_fpm_origin',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD ABSTRACT: Weline Server (WLS) managed Nginx supports TWO public-edge origin modes via `wls.edge.nginx.origin_mode`: `wls` (default — `proxy_pass` → loopback WLS Workers / Session / Memory) and `fpm` (assisted deploy — `fastcgi_pass` → local php-fpm → `{BP}/pub/index.php`). REQUIRED: (1) Switch ONLY with `php bin/w server:origin:set fpm|wls` (optional `--fpm-listen=HOST:PORT|unix:/path`); FORBID inventing a parallel switch path or hand-editing live managed conf as the mode source of truth. (2) FPM still uses PROJECT-ISOLATED managed Nginx generated by WLS—FORBID injecting site conf into system `/etc/nginx`. (3) FPM does NOT require Workers/Session/Memory; after a successful set to fpm the business plane MUST be stopped while keeping Nginx (`server:stop --keep-nginx`, also done by origin:set); switching back to wls REQUIRES a subsequent manual `php bin/w server:start` (origin:set MUST NOT auto-start Workers). (4) TLS/Local CA / host catalog MUST follow the SAME path as WLS origin—FORBID dropping certificates or falling back to weak `server_name=_` + localhost leaf when origin_mode=fpm. (5) `server:start` MUST NOT silently change `origin_mode` and MUST NOT silently install Nginx. (6) Agent MUST NOT assume “WLS = Workers only” when the user asks PHP-FPM / fpm origin / 协助部署 FPM. Authority: `app/code/Weline/Server/doc/WLS模式部署指南.md` (回源模式：WLS Workers vs PHP-FPM). Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/wls-managed-nginx-supports-fpm-origin.mdc`. Complements `runtime_status_query_local_first` and managed-Nginx install/start gates.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Server/doc/WLS模式部署指南.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'production_http_probe_forbids_agent_local_curl',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD ABSTRACT: When the Agent must probe HTTP connectivity / status / live HTML of a PRODUCTION or public CDN-fronted storefront Host (user already authorized 线上/生产/公网站点), FORBIDDEN to curl/wget/httpie/fetch that public Host (or its apex/www FQDN) from the Agent local workstation shell (Cursor host / IDE agent egress)—non-browser UA and WLS path_scan/attack_guard can shared_ban the shared egress IP and Forbidden the operator’s own browser. REQUIRED: (1) SSH to the site-cabinet primary Host (`websites/<site>/README.md` 主用 SSH Host / SSH MCP profile) then curl `http://127.0.0.1/...` or `https://127.0.0.1/...` with `Host:` (and SNI when needed); for live HTML/robots/sitemap acceptance also append the install-level FPC pierce stamp from `generated/framework/fpc_pierce_secret` as `w_fpc_pierce=<secret>` in the same SSH command, never printing/logging the secret; OR (2) SSH MCP equivalent on that profile. On shared_ban Forbidden: `php bin/w server:security:unblock --ip=<client>` or `--clear-all` on that instance (after backup/ops judgment)—do NOT “fix” by more local public curls. EXEMPT / complementary: local acceptance Hosts (`*.test.weline.com`, `127.0.0.1`/`localhost` project ports) remain curl-probeable per `browser_operator_fail_closed_release`; host Browser WB-OP with real browser UA is not this ban path. Complements `runtime_status_query_local_first` (default local queries) and SSH host-mapping rules. Skill: `production_http_probe` / `weline-production-http-probe`. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/production-http-probe-forbids-agent-local-curl.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'theme_update_matches_site_cabinet',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD ABSTRACT: When the user asks for a theme deploy/update (主题更新, 更新某主题, 发布主题, 发布某主题, theme update, or theme:update—legacy theme:upgrade—as an ops request—not CSS authoring). 「发布主题」 is the same utterance as 「更新主题」, the Agent MUST resolve the named theme or site alias against the local website-cabinet relationship card `websites/<site>/关系.md` (one card per site: SSH host, app root, theme register name, local design path) and MUST cross-check the app root against that site `server.md` (server.md wins on host/path). The match MUST be unique and complete (host + app root + theme path all filled, and not contradicted by server.md). THEN copy ONLY that theme directory to `{app_root}/app/design/{Vendor}/{theme}/` via rsync/scp with NO `--delete`, THEN on that host run `php bin/w theme:update -t <theme>` (generation switch: build new batch → verify → flip pointer; no maintenance mode). Run `php bin/w setup:upgrade` BEFORE it ONLY when the theme is newly registered, new layout files were added, or the module registration surface changed. FORBID: guessing the host from a nickname or SSH-alias collision; copying a theme onto a different site app root; copying when the card says no production host or the app root is unverified; skipping the copy and only running a local theme:update; `rsync --delete`. A local design directory with no cabinet card is not a site. This utterance authorizes theme sync for the matched site only—it does not waive `runtime_status_query_local_first` for unrelated status queries, and live HTML probes still follow `production_http_probe_forbids_agent_local_curl` (SSH then 127.0.0.1 + Host). COMPLEMENT `user_utterance_commit_ships_dev_and_sites`: the 「提交」 pipeline republishes themes already on the server and MUST NOT upload `app/design` unless the user separately asks to upload; THIS rule is that separate upload utterance. EXAMPLES ONLY (not the rule body): 「更新汉服主题」resolves via the cabinet card whose theme name is hanfu, not via the SSH alias hanfu. Authority: 规则/40 §9 + websites/SKILL.md mode D. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/theme-update-matches-site-cabinet.mdc`.',
