            [
                'id' => 'framework_demos_live_in_weline_demo',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD ABSTRACT: Framework/feature VISUAL verification demos (DEV marker eyeball pages, mechanism demos, “open a page so I can see the mark”, Agent-built throwaway storefront demo pages for humans) MUST live under module `Weline_Demo` (`app/code/Weline/Demo`) as Frontend routes—add a page there, do NOT spawn a new one-off `*Demo` / `*DupDemo` module under `app/code`, and FORBID parking such demos inside owning business modules (Checkout/Theme/Cart/…). HARD: `Weline_Demo` is LOCAL-ONLY / gitignored (`/app/code/Weline/Demo/` in repo `.gitignore`)—FORBID committing that tree (or re-adding it to Git). Formal automated tests (PHPUnit/contracts/Playwright e2e) STILL belong in the owning module `test/`/`Test/`—this rule is only for human/Agent visual demo surfaces. EXEMPT: `Weline_WidgetDemo` (dedicated widget registry/default-injection fixture module; MAY stay in Git); website/theme seed kits (`website_concept_seed_not_in_modules`); content_ops. Positive example: same-slot duplicate DEV red-outline page at `/weline_demo/frontend/slot-dup`. Host alwaysApply mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/framework-demos-live-in-weline-demo.mdc`. Complements global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host + learning_rule_extraction_must_be_abstract.',
