            [
                'id' => 'session_learning_knowledge_conflict_gate',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY session-learning knowledge gate: (1) Classify user asks—durable framework/process constraints that should bind future work are KNOWLEDGE (learning intent); one-off delivery tasks are REQUIREMENT. A requirement that changes framework architecture/policy MAY ALSO mint a knowledge candidate after it lands. (2) Cursor/Codex learning hooks feed Learning SQLite; Agent MUST treat prepare_project.agent_guidance.learning_conflicts and resolve_task_context rules from validated_session_learning as binding project memory. (3) Before edits that would contradict validated/contested learning or open contradictions: STOP and wait for explicit user decision—do not silently override. (4) HARD user-facing conflict report (裁决可读): whenever hooks/prepare report contested>0 or open contradictions, OR the Agent must ask the user to adjudicate, EACH conflict MUST be explained in plain Chinese sufficient for a non-agent reader to decide—per item include: 争议主题(一句); 甲方主张(经验标题+reusable_rule 白话，可附 id); 乙方主张(同上); 为何被标成冲突(真对立 / 近重复误配 / 与当前任务相撞); 选 A/B 的影响; ≥2 可执行选项 + 推荐. FORBID reporting only contradiction/experience IDs, only counts (「contested=2」), or bare「有冲突请裁决」without substance. SessionStart / prepare learning_conflicts notices inherit the same report duty before continuing engineering that could override knowledge. (5) When the user confirms a knowledge rule, record evidence/outcome via learningctl when available; when they supersede/merge, mark contested/revised/resolved and proceed only after decision. (6) Obey learning_rule_extraction_must_be_abstract when minting or promoting knowledge. Content-ops skill turns exempt from this gate as a blocker, but if the Agent still surfaces a learning conflict it must use the same clear report schema. SELF-EVOLUTION LEDGER (host mirror `~/.cursor/rules/learning-ledger-self-evolution.mdc`): every engineering session MUST load learnings at start (`prepare_project.agent_guidance.learning_conflicts`, `resolve_task_context.rules`; cross-project workflow lessons via `php ~/.dsh/bin/learning.php check --project=<p>`), record reusable evidence-backed rules at closeout (`learningctl evidence/outcome`; host `add --rule --evidence`), supersede conflicting entries with history kept (`supersede --id --by --reason`; MCP contested/revised + user decision), warn before acting on a major non-conforming request (learning id + risk + alternative), and treat a user-specified approach as highest authority (record `source=user`, supersede conflicts). FORBID silent overwrite, one-off facts as rules, or skipping the start check.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
