            [
                'id' => 'social_scope_mailbox_for_platform_register',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD ABSTRACT utterance: when the user mentions 融媒体/社媒 or a social platform (YouTube/Facebook/Instagram/X/TikTok and peers) together with register, publish, lookup, or that site’s media accounts, the Agent MUST Read skill weline-social-platform-register before acting. Resolve the named website, then read THAT site’s Weline_Social accounts and pick the named platform. LOOKUP: if the account exists, report it and use it; if missing, report that—do not silently register. CONTENT PUBLISH (post, image, or video): Read skill weline-social-content-publish. Walk only that site cabinet in-use social accounts, one by one; do not invent platforms, and do not stop the rest when one account cannot post. REGISTER only when that name resolves to a website cabinet that is already online: `websites/<site>/server.md` MUST name the primary SSH host, app root, and official hostname, AND an on-server probe of that official host (SSH to the cabinet host, then curl 127.0.0.1 with Host) returns 200/302/308. No server.md, not launched, or official site unreachable → report and STOP; do not ensure a mailbox or open a browser. FORBIDDEN agent-local curl of the public FQDN. The mailbox domain MUST be that official hostname, not a local test host. If the cabinet is online and the site already has the platform account, report it and stop; if not, require that live mail domain. Domain/post office not ready → report and STOP (do not invent a domain or a second email). Domain ready and mailbox missing → ensure social-{websiteCode}@that domain. BEFORE any browser signup, probeScopeSocialMailbox must show the social mailbox can deliver to that domain’s contact@ inbox; unconfirmed/failed probe → STOP. Signup uses the operator’s Google Chrome (chrome-devtools), that mailbox only, and the platform https signup URL. Ordinary on-page clicks are allowed. A human-check (checkbox, image challenge, slider, or “I am not a robot”) MUST be handled in place: screenshot that region, read the image, and click the recognized target with browser coordinates, then continue signup. FORBIDDEN to stop and ask the user when a human-check appears. A page-script click on a cross-origin captcha iframe shell does not count as clicking the checkbox. FORBIDDEN: captcha-solving services. If that screenshot-and-click attempt still does not pass, record the platform and continue the next one; do not halt the rest of the list, and do not claim the signup finished. When the utterance covers more than one platform, any other stuck platform (mobile-app-only signup, missing parent account for that platform only, or a browser already signed into someone else\'s account) is recorded and the Agent continues the next platform; FORBIDDEN to halt the rest of the list. FORBIDDEN to sign out someone else\'s account to register this site. A single named platform that is stuck for a reason other than a human-check still asks the user in that Chrome window only after the in-place attempt. Site-level gates (no server.md, origin down, tab group cannot be created, admin social page unseen or scope mismatch) still STOP the whole run. FORBIDDEN: a different email per platform, hardcoded mailbox/password, AppleScript activate. Host mirror: `~/.cursor/rules/social-scope-mailbox-register.mdc`.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/30-后端与数据.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'browser_automation_uses_ego',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY browser-automation default = ego lite. For opening sites, clicking, filling forms, screenshots, page extraction, UI/interaction acceptance (WB-OP) the Agent MUST use ego: on DSH call ego_doctor first, then ego_recall (known site) → ego_run (one script per task) → ego_learn (promote a step that worked) → ego_site_run (reuse) and ego_handoff when a human must act; when the host plugin is not loaded, use the `ego-browser` CLI per the ego-browser skill (`ego-browser skill` then `ego-browser nodejs`). FORBID launching Chrome / puppeteer / Playwright / headless Chromium for exploration, clicking, screenshots, or UI acceptance; FORBID treating “plugin not restarted” as a reason to fall back to those. EXCEPTIONS: (1) formal repository e2e still runs only via `php bin/w e2e:run` / repo playwright.config (e2e_playwright_formal_runner_only) — ego does not replace the e2e suite; (2) the user explicitly asks for Chrome / Chrome extension / the Weline profile — then the Chrome contracts (google_chrome_reuse_before_connect, browser_tab_group_identity) apply. All acceptance rules still bind: browser_operator_self_test, browser_cache_disabled_on_open (FPC pierce), browser_operator_fail_closed_release (curl ≤5s before navigate, release on hang). Install (DSH): `dsh plugin --profile <name> add -w @dshworks/dsh-ego-browser`, then restart DSH; tools = ego_doctor / ego_recall / ego_run / ego_site_run / ego_learn / ego_forget / ego_handoff. Authority: 规则/00 §8b; host rule `~/.dsh/AGENTS.md`「浏览器操作默认 ego」.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'no_script_batch_replace',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY HARD (user-designated 2026-10-28): Editing files is hands-on, ONE file per targeted edit — FORBIDDEN: script/command batch replace or batch rewrite of files at ANY scale (`sed -i`, `awk -i`, `perl -pi`, `xargs` + editor commands, `find … -exec` rewrites, `grep -rl | xargs sed`, `php -r` / `python -c` walk-and-rewrite loops, generated one-shot migration scripts that rewrite many files, replace-all macros, editor global find-replace run by the Agent). Correct loop, repeated N times: host Read the CURRENT on-disk file → targeted Edit/Write/ApplyPatch on that ONE file → re-read to verify → next file; large sets are batched with per-batch reporting. READ-ONLY sweeps stay allowed: grep/rg/find/diff for locating, counting, and acceptance comparison — but every hit you then modify still goes through the per-file edit loop; never "grep a list, change all with one command". WHY: regex match scope is uncontrollable — one bad pattern corrupts hundreds of files at once (content loss, encoding/newline damage, other-session in-flight edits swept in, per [preserve_dirty_workspace]) and breakage often stays invisible until later; a wrong per-file edit damages exactly one file and is caught immediately. EXCEPTION (all steps required): the user explicitly names script/batch operation in their own words this turn → first back up EVERY target under `<repo-root>/dev/backup/<path-relative-to-root>.<timestamp>` (see backup-dir rule), dry-run ONE file and show its diff to the user, expand only after they confirm, then spot-verify per file and list affected files in closeout. Violation grading: batch-replacing files via script is a violation EVEN IF the result happens to be correct — STOP, keep the scene, report a 「批量替换违规记录」 (files + whether backed up + disposition); never mask it with git rollback ([concurrent_session_commit_hygiene] forbids stash/checkout/clean/reset). Complements preserve_dirty_workspace (shell-write bypass of CAS), concurrent_session_commit_hygiene, machine_shared_side_effects_require_workspace_scope; dual-write host mirrors per global_rules_dual_write_mcp_and_host: personal agent global mirror `~/.dsh/AGENTS.md`「禁止脚本批量替换」(user-global `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` only where that surface is still live—do not hand-author into a retired directory)。Authority: 规则/00 §4.4.',
                'doc' => 'app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/规则/00-MCP调用与会话.md',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 'module_doc_forbids_ephemeral_work_artifacts',
                'summary' => 'MANDATORY: Module `app/code/*/doc/` is for durable module knowledge ONLY—三文档契约 (`需求.md`/`功能现状.md`/`开发日志.md`), README, lasting guides/API/architecture docs, `doc/ai/skills/**`, durable feature specs at owning-module `doc/开发/spec/{slug}.md`, and lasting charters already published as product knowledge. FORBIDDEN under any module `doc/` (esp. `doc/开发/` root): `plan.md` / `task.md` / `*-plan.md` / `*-task.md`; dated investigation dumps (`*排查*`, timing/perf session notes); one-off bugfix notes (`*修复*.md` that are not durable guides); disposable checklists/smoke logs/汇审 scratch; `doc/开发/session/**` / `doc/开发/team/**` wave folders; ops briefs. Those MUST go under repository-root `dev/` (gitignored): SESSION/plan/task=`dev/session/{slug}.md` (or `dev/session/...`); team minutes=`dev/team/{slug}/`; throwaways=`dev/tmp/`. Durable conclusions may be summarized into owning-module `doc/开发日志.md`—FORBID parking the full ephemeral dump in module doc. Historical files already under module `doc/开发/team|session` may remain read-only for continuity—NEW writes MUST use `dev/`. Complements requirement_session_dashboard / plan_content_focus_only / engineering_team_for_new_requirements; do not “archive” temp ops into module doc to make them look durable.',
            ],
        ];
